



return {
	["Test Entry"] = "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.",
	["Test Entry 2"] = "testing smaller amount of text this time",
	Omagatoki = "The woodlands of the Heightser Plateau have a fearsome reputation for being cursed. Its peats stain the souls of the sinners that perish within, preventing their reincarnation. Cursed to forever wander the spirit realm.\n\nThe eternal walk changes them. Many repent, many find solace in with their fellow spirits. A few still wish to breach the mortal realm, either to return to their old life, or to conquer it.\n\nWhat they don't know is how flimsy the boundary between man and ghost truly is. Once a year the River Hei bursts its banks in its annual flooding, allowing the spirits that dwell within to enter the mortal realm once more.\n\nWelcome to the Ōmagatoki, where the Yourei walk freely.",
	Meebozo = "The Meeboids took on many different forms during their evolution throughout millenias. While still on the Spaceship Xargasdon, meeboids used to be more elusive creatures that merely scavenged and hid to make due, avoiding many of the predators that sought to feast on their bountiful vitality.\n\nWith the shifting ecosystem having gotten rid of many of their old predators, many meeboids shed their ancestry to pursue a much more lively tradition. Some, however, still hold onto their ancestral traits.",
	["Titanwarped Terror"] = "The effects of the Titans ravaging Robloxia to find the brick couldn't be overstated.\nAs colossal beings whose existence predates Robloxia, composed of more studs than Robloxia itself, their mere existence warped its flora and fauna. Trees whispered foul tales, creatures grew monstrous in size, mountaintops started to float... Yet people gained access to more primal forms of stud magic as the titanic studs irradiated their bodies too.",
	["Plea for Guidance"] = "The death and destruction of the Alpha Wars followed by the abusive use of the Alpha Brick destabilised Robloxia's people and climate; Purple stones rained from the sky smashing into everything. Oceans boiled. Animals grew violent. Day and night got faster and faster. \n\nFearing the apocalypse, the people of Robloxia turned to anything that could save them as their pleas to Telamon fell on silent ears. \nThe instability of Robloxia, feasting on the collective desire of the people, answered their prayers.",
	["Heated Debate"] = "There are many Javionese who consider Yuéliáng's compassion as a sign of cowardice -- choosing to pick less extreme options out of fear of backlash or worse. In truth, she believed in the pursuit of mediation and understanding. The Paraselenes needed to adapt with the changing world, lest be left behind in the pages of old. A lack of integrity and allies could not be fixed with their lunar magic without breaking their oaths.\n\nA belief she held onto passionately. A belief that the energy within the fallen satellite planted its festering emotions into.",
	["Artemis Carter"] = "Eisenhower's secret laboratory whirred to life as he flicked his left switch underneath his worktable. His lover's body was splayed across its sterile length, slowly putrefying. He hoped the embalming would keep his husband-to-be's defilement at bay for longer.\n\nHis fiancé stirred, then jolted wide awake. He seemed confused that he was alive and indeed his existence was a confusion. Eisenhower had done the impossible, the unimaginable: Total recovery of the dead, an act only rumoured to be done since the Korblox thousands of years ago, discovered and mastered within days. Such was the incredible genius of the scientist that now watched rigor mortis leave his lover's body, watched the body become a man once again.\n\"Why am I here, Eisen?\" Oh, to hear that buttery baritone voice again! Eisenhower's heart was reanimated in tandem with his lover.\n\"I-I couldn't live with you, Artie. I-I saved you.\"\n\"Saved? Didn't I... Die?\"\n\"We can work the details out later. It always works out in the end, right?\"\n\"There's nothing you can't invent yourself out of, is there?\"\n\nThe two of them embraced, living and undead together. The start - no, the continuation - of a beautiful union.\nSuch is the first recorded use of the Necroenzyme. It's a shame such an earnest invention caused such devastation.",
	["Corporate Spy"] = "\"The ability to reanimate people, to undo their death as if they never died. That's powerful, Eisie.\"\nEisenhower cocked his head, a brave smirk cut across his face. It's good to be smart.\n\"I know. No one knows about it but us. I'll ensure it stays that way.\"\n\"They'll ask questions if they see me, though?\"\n\"I-I'll close the windows. We rarely get visitors. You'll be fine. We'll be fine. Haha.\"\n\"I dunno... You sure you've thought this through?\" Artemis' voice reeked of concern.\n\"You want to go back to being dead? Sounds like a fun night out.\"\nEisenhower chuckled. Artemis hesitantly joined him.\n\n\"After all, no one ever visits the weird lab maniac on the outskirts of Bloxburg. People think I'm a freak, but not you. You kept me around when no one else would. It's only fair I return the favour. I'm cognisant of my invention's applications. They will not be exploited. No one will know.\"\n\nIn the corner of Eisenhower's lab, an intruder took a silent photograph. An enzyme that can reanimate the dead? The government would love to know about this.",
	["Dinosaur of Xargasdon"] = "(Arkhive Hive Terminal Chatlogs 23/1-20\nCT : So\nCT : This here's the spot?\nNA : Yup \nNA : that's is where we got some real strong tectonic signals, along with some interesting ruins\nNA : looks like xargasdonian architecture, if the records are correct\nCT : I mean, yeah\nCT : You told me that the place had artifacts from the Knights of the Splintered Skies\nNA : oh yeah i did\nCT : So, the source is coming from the deep rock formations?\nNA : right you are\nNA : seems like they're in a constant rhythm, like something big is breathing\nNA : like REALLY BIG\nCT : Alright, I'll just go play one of those calling signals\nNA : yea sure\nNA : see anything yet?\nCT : Uh, yeah!\nNA : what is it?\nCT : A REALLY BIG dinosaur.",
	["Corporate Smuggler"] = "Days passed. Artemis got comfortable with this new state of existence. There were problems, of course; Being technically a corpse, he had to constantly be injected with the Necroenzyme in order to stay alive. But there were benefits. Being alive. Not becoming mush when a bookcase falls on you. Never dying... That last one was a bit scary. He could live with Eisenhower forever, but the affection while mutual was finite. Could their love transcend millennia? What would the world be like in a thousand years time?\nStill, if he ever wanted to die, all he had to do was nothing. The existential dread can wait until later.\n\nEisenhower and Artemis locked eyes and arms together several times that week. They spent so much time together, so much time on each other. They were the only thing that mattered.",
	["Hazing Ritual"] = "The bloodied corpse reconstituted itself. No matter how many beatings her father took, the enzyme made it impossible for him to die. Impossible for him to leave this torture. Kingrin's sledgehammer was more than a shaft of metal in his hands; It was a paintbrush to create violent, bestial, carnal art.\n\nThe new recruit shied away from her father. Kingrin growled.\n\"He hurt you, pup. This is what you do to those who hurt the family, no matter who.\"\n\"E-ven so. This is too-\"\n\"An attack on one is an attack on us all! Will you act like this when one of your kin is attacked? No. You'll bear your fangs.\"\nKingrin passed a small spiked mace to the recruit.\n\n\"Demonstrate you can protect us.\"",
	["Corporate Marketeer"] = "\"YOU SAID NO ONE WOULD KNOW!\" Artemis grabbed Eisenhower's ears, forcing him to stare at the television.\n\"EXPLAIN THIS. EXPLAIN THIS!\"\n\"I-I checked the security logs! There's nothing since you were resurrected!\"\n\n\"And before that?\"\nEisenhower dreaded the answer. He calmly turned around, approached his monitor. Artemis could tell how unhappy and surprised his typing was.\n\nHe turned back to Artemis with a heavy sigh.\n\"Guess I'll be inventing a memory-wiping serum next.\"",
	["Booming Boomer"] = "\"Have you gotten the reports, Mayor Astarossa?\"\n\"...Yes, I have.\"\n\"What do you suppose we do about it?\"\n\"...\"\n\"Mayor Astarossa?\"\n\"I'll draft a bill regulating proper usage for the serum. I expect you to review it upon release.\"\n\"Of course, Sir.\"\n\"Very well.\"\n\"Are we prepared for next year's election campaign?\"",
	["Corporate Killer"] = "(Excerpt from Brick Heights, Issue #104 - Farewell)\nDear citizens of Bloxburg, we apologise.\nWe set this magazine up to document the Necroenzyme's extraordinary properties and use in our fair city. It was going great! Two years have passed, and the promises made by Apollo Scott and Astarossa Van Buren have fallen to shreds.\n\nWe have just been bought out by the Astral Faith, and this will be our last paper before editorial freedom is stripped from us. It is better to be silent than a mouthpiece for propaganda, and thus this is the last you'll hear from us. \n\nImmortality has corrupted us in ways we could never fathom.\nLaw has been replaced with chaos on the streets. Power is in the hands of corrupt gangsters who control death itself. Times were great when the enzyme flowed freely; Our greatest folly was failing to ensure its use was sustainable.\n\nWe've served this town diligently. Get out if you can. \nGoodbye.",
	["Parking Lot Attendant"] = "Before his legendary bravery in the face of Zanzel's tyranny in 432 AD, David Crissbach was a commoner struggling to make ends meet for his family. He worked in Hallows' pits at a food stand until 421, returning to Bloxburg to help out his father's ailing construction trade. \n\nDuring a nightshift in his sidehustle as a parking lot attendant, Crissbach intervened in an armed robbery only to see the attacker dismembered and the victim oozing green, both unharmed.\nAlthough previously dismissing all the rumours of zombies running around, such undeniable evidence shook Crissbach to his core; He reported it to the police a mere hour before Apollo Scott's announcement of the necroenzyme-assisted capture of Thec Hiller.\n\nYou can't escape the future.",
	["Long-Lost Son"] = "\"Oh, Dr. Sarah. What brings you here?\"\n\"S-Sorry for coming here in the middle of the night. I... I just want to talk about your son.\"\n\"...James?\"\n\"Doctor, you don't look so good... Do you feel bad about what happened to him? Please, we alrea-\"\n\"N-No! You don't need to be sad about it anymore!\"\n\n\"...what?\"\n\n\"Your son! I-I... I brought him back!\"",
	["Offroad Motorbike"] = "An early prototype in the NeFoCo's enzyme recipe, Caitlin Nixon was reanimated but unable to properly regenerate. Equipped with a robot chassis, Caitlin required several new tools in order to continue her work as an archaeologist.\nAngry at the NeFoCo for what she considered a botched reanimation, Caitlin asked Eisenhower for advice, both of them unaware she was powered with his stolen necroenzyme recipe.\nSo Eisenhower agreed to give her and her organisation the Arkhive some experimental technology; In addition to the speed, solar panels, and charging station so Caitlin can keep recharging, This bike is able to smell the ground around it as it drives and send those signals to Caitlin, allowing her to sample the age and toxicity of various samples.\n\nDue to how little enzyme is needed to sustain a chassis, under Apate's suggestions the NeFoCo dropped the technology in favour of the much more efficient Zoombas.",
	["Eisenhower Dwit"] = "A legendary figure who would go on to become a quadheron prophesied in Ancient Stirrings, propelled to unwilling stardom by the invention of the endoloco (a rediscovery of the automobile) in 211AD.\nEisenhower was bullied relentlessly as a child for his awkwardness by his peers and parents, to the point he gave up socialisation entirely and spent his childhood reading, instilling a calm yet zealous all-consuming desire for omniscience in him.\n\nHaving spent every waking moment of his life reading and learning, when the magician Artemis Carter took a shine to him the friendship quickly turned into a relationship, into an obsession.\nRefusing to have his one chance at happiness taken away from him, Artemis' death propelled the inventor to play god and create his most infamous invention.\n\nHERRUS' NOTES: Eisenhower was meant to be called \"Erlenmeyer\" in reference to the flask, but a botched spelling caused him - And eventually most hexaherons of Necrosyndicates - To be named after US presidents.",
	["United Front"] = "Hailing from a cluster of Javionese immigrants that arrived at Bloxburg shortly after the Overlay, the Lordbreakers are used to being at the bottom rung of society and resent those who so trivially squander their wealth and power.\n\nNaturally it wasn't long before the Lordbreakers, already a radical activist organisation championing the most vulnerable members of society, also championed the rights of these thinking, feeling zombies. They wouldn't be in this situation without the enzyme and the Lordbreakers vow to make it illegal to inject living people with the enzyme to zombify them.\n\nPeople are not tools, and their lives are not toys or experiments. You have nothing to lose but your chains.",
	["Harrowing Rejection"] = "WHY?\nWHY WEREN'T THEY HAPPY?\nI BROUGHT THEIR SON BACK! I FIXED HIS LUNG TUMOR!\nWHY'D THEY START... SCREAMING?\nTHEY WERE SUPPOSED TO BE HAPPY RIGHT? THAT'S HOW PEOPLE FEEL WHEN THEY SEE THEIR LOVED ONES GET BETTER, RIGHT?\nI TRIED MAKING UP FOR EVERYONE I FAILED TO SAVE! I MADE THEM BETTER! SO WHY? GOD... GODDAMNIT!\nWHY CAN'T I FEEL BETTER?\nWHY CAN'T I JUST FEEL FINE AGAIN?\nWHY CAN'T I JUST MAKE IT GO AWAY?????\n...\nMake it... Go away...\nRight...\n\nM-Maybe I can just...\nMake it go away...",
	["Tear and Reshape"] = "\"You sure about this? What about the families who were planning funerals with the bodies?\"\n\"Look, what's important is making sure our morgue's transported somewhere safer until this whole bloomin' fiasco about resurrection blows over. We can't risk anyone barging into there and making a mess.\"\n\"I... I see.\"\n\"We've already got a lot on our hands already, even moreso with Sarah, Gavin and Corie on their breaks, even MORESO with companies selling the necroenzyme like a fizzy drink. Bloomin' opportunists... don't they realize they're messing with society as a whole?\"\n\n(The surgeon opens the door to the morgue.)\n\n\"...Oh, crap.\"\n\"Wh-what is it, Dr. Grey?!\"\n\n(The nurse gasps at the sight.)\n\n\"T-The morgue...! It's... it's-!\"\n\n\"Completely empty.\"",
	["Portable Translator"] = "(Greenbelt Ranger Report circa 45-03)\n\"Begin audio report. Time, five past eighteen.\"\n\"Gharial poaching has increased 204% this past month - suspected to be caused by increased necroenzyme usage in Bloxburg.\"\n\"Noted slight increase in disappearance of non-crocodile fauna - will need further investigation.\"\n\"Moving forward - expecting escort for Arkhive member Nina Hellensoft.\"\n\"Report over-\"\n\n(door creaking open)\n\"W-What the hell?\"\n\n\n\"Hey, cosplayer! What the hell are you doing here?! This is a restricted area! Get out before I have t-\"\n(glass breaking)\n\"WHAT THE H-\"\n(sound of machine breaking)\n\n(End of Recording)",
	["Apollo Scott, Visionary"] = "A mild-mannered 16 year old, one of the hexaherons prophesised in Necrosyndicates.\n\nBorn to two millionaires, Apollo Scott’s parents were murdered in cold blood in front of him when he was four. The incident paralyzed him from the legs down.\nSwearing revenge, Scott delved relentlessly into forensic science and robotics, his studies paying off a decade later when Scott’s novel investigations were instrumental in taking down the serial killer known as the Robloxcity Ripper.\nLaunching the NecroForensics Corporation off his relations with the police, Apollo Scott was the first to capitalise on the Necroenzyme and it’s made him and his investors a small fortune. Using the necroenzyme to revolutionise funeral services, crime investigations, and robotics, Apollo wants nothing more than to help bloxburg and wider robloxia.\nIt takes many people to run a corporation; Teams of inventors, accountants, and marketeers working together for profit.\n\nFew of them share Apollo’s heart of gold…",
	["Bloxburg Mayor Astarossa"] = "The stoic mayor of Bloxburg, one of the hexaherons prophesised in Necrosyndicates.\n\nHaving won every election for the past 40 years on the back of a hardcore voter base who follow their every word, Astarossa controls Bloxburg’s government; Despite elections being free and fair, Bloxburg could be mistaken for a dictatorship.\nVeterans of the tail end of the Demon Wars 50 years prior, Astarossa and their voter base are in their twilight years and they dislike their newer voters for wanting critical infrastructure reforms that the older voter base hate. Eager to keep their loyal voterbase alive, as well as put Bloxburg on the map as an economic powerhouse, Astarossa sets up a public healthcare facility in Bloxburg’s town square, giving Bloxburg’s residents free injections to prevent death.\n\nAstarossa is keenly aware of how fragile a democracy can be when the ruler so easily controls who lives and dies…\n\nHERRUS' NOTES: Astarossa was radically redesigned. Initially he was going to be a cult-like priest who brainwashed people with the enzyme. Deciding this was too fantastical especially with Caitlin and Fl00fy, the Culture Industry turned him into a mayor.",
	["Kingrin, Surrounded by Familey"] = "A violent yet fiercely protective mob boss, one of the hexaherons prophesised in Necrosyndicates.\n\nWhat started as a protection pact between orphans in the rundown slums of Bloxburg’s Povvo Street has turned into the most fearsome gang in all of Robloxia. With tireless vigilance, “Kingrin” will stop at nothing to improve his familey’s lives, even if that means decapitating their foes in broad daylight. The condemnation of Bloxburg doesn’t stop people joining his familey - The camaraderie between wayward souls is intense, for there is no safer place in Bloxburg than Kingrin’s side and nowhere more dangerous than in front of him.\nAlthough it feels like it, Kingrin can’t do everything; His weaker familey sometimes get picked off to taunt him. With the Necroenzyme, he can keep those people safe, and make his revenge far more brutal; Kingrin's studio is home to endless screams as those who hurt his familey are revived and killed, over and over and over and over and over...\n\nWhen you see a crowd grinning in the night, make sure to grin back.",
	["Caitlin, Paladin of Nature"] = "A cheerful archaeologist with a colourful Fife-Scottish accent, one of the hexaherons prophesised in Necrosyndicates.\n\nAfter her original body succumbed to a chronic disease, she lives her life in the forests near Bloxburg as a robot. From afar, she stays in contact with the Arkhive, a research group composed of her old students and research peers as they study data about New Robloxia and its history, as well as remnants of the ages before the Robloxian Overlay. She’s especially interested in the days before the Dwarvern Meteor of 0BC.\nDespite her isolation in the wilderness of Bloxburg’s Greenbelt, Caitlin is content in living out her life and hobby as a historian. She enjoys taking care of the local fauna, seeing them as her friends.\nThrough her contacts, Caitlin caught wind of a serum which could restore a person who had died in generally healthy condition and stable mind. Caitlin dismisses the potential hazards of spreading the Necroenzyme, only brainstorming about how the serum could be used to establish contact with and interview old figures of the past. Optimistic, she collects a supply of the serum through her suppliers, ready to speak to the primary sources of her history books.\n\nFor all her intellect, she didn’t consider how many desperate people would want an immortality serum...",
	Fl00fy_Bonez = "An organiser of hedonistic raves, one of the hexaherons prophesised in Necrosyndicates.\n\nWhen masking her authentic self, Sarah Greene Bailey is an esteemed surgeon for the Bloxburg Messiah Infirmary. An empath who has failed to save her patients from impossible odds one too many times, absorbing the grief of their families and becoming depressed, she copes by reconnecting with her teenage years: By attending raves, partying the night away, drowning out her negativity.\n\nAn ardent hedonist and utilitarian, she believes that pleasure and pain are the only things that matter in life, and wants to remove as much suffering from the world as she can. Although she starts by resurrecting long-lost failed patients, their families naturally reject their kin being turned into zombies, and this shocks her into insanity. Living a dual life as Fl00fy_Bonez, she secretly assembles PLURRAL, a gang of unthinking zombies and those who wish to be such, capable only of feeling pleasure.\nNo more pain, no more thoughts, no more death. Only pleasure. FOREVER.",
	["McKayla, Bane of Hierarchy"] = "A passionate yet bitter teenage activist, one of the hexaherons prophesised in Necrosyndicates.\n\nThe daughter of Javionese immigrants after the Robloxian Overlay, McKayla Newman is used to fending for herself. As the most well-known member of the Lordbreakers, a radical activist organisation, McKayla is a frequent thorn in the side of Astarossa as she exposes what’s in her mind deep-rooted inequalities in the city.\nThe current state of Bloxburg is already messy, with Povvo Street’s slums juxtaposed with Sfothwir Square’s opulence. With several organisations experimenting with a previously-unknown, untested necromancy substance, The Lordbreakers fear for the poor and the exploited, and thus their actions have intensified. They want to make the enzyme illegal.\n\nWith her parents telling her stories of Biggs Cradshaw's tyranny, she is deeply aware of what happens when rulers so easily choose who lives and dies.",
	["Morgue Merchant"] = "The first group to manufacture the enzyme at an industrial scale and the one with the largest stockpile, the NecroForensics Corporation attempted to corner the market on immortality. Their wide spread of products touching on robotics, funeral services, cleaning, architecture, and even military hardware have made the already wealthy child progeny Apollo Scott more so.\n\nApollo believes this is his chance to make the world a better place. It's his mission to improve society, and his work is doing just that.\nStill, even a small corporation like his employ others, especially to round out the skills the awkwardly-mannered inventor lacks.\nIt's hard to ensure they have the same ideals as his...",
	["Join the Cause"] = "Once it enters the body, the Necroenzyme kills its host within two hours. All heart and brain functions cease organic function, kept going indefinitely by the very poison that stopped it. There are no adverse affects as long as you keep taking the enzyme, but you'll die quickly once it leaves your system.\n\nThe Mayor sees this as a great opportunity, as the holy grail of all vaccines, as a solution to Death itself. He's built public enzyme houses where people can freely, safely take their regular dose of immortality. It's the right thing to do.\n\nIt's also effective on the campaign trail. You wouldn't want your immortality dole to stop, would you?",
	["Found Familey"] = "Homeless, Fatherless, Futureless, the lowest and most vulnerable members of society flock to the Smiley Familey. Offering free food, clothing, housing to those who join, the most ruthless gang in robloxia ensures that no one slips through the cracks or is ignored.\n\nTheir brutality is not for mere show; It's free advertisement the media'll plaster for the weak, and a price of entry keeping out those unable to fulfill the smiley's social obligations.\n\nThe misspelt name was originally used by the gang's early detractors, only to be embraced. There truly is a familey here.",
	["Greenbelt Surveyor"] = "Bloxburg's Greenbelt is a wide stretch of countryside which Astarossa has designated a protected wildlife reserve. No new buildings can be kept on it to protect the rich biodiversity and fossil record, stretching back from the days of the Temple of Telamon.\n\nThe Arkhive™ is the corporation Astarossa created to protect the wildlife and he regrets it. What used to be a useful mouthpiece for his propaganda has turned into a scathing Scottish critic, lambasting his inability to protect the Greenbelt from poachers and invasive species.\n\nThe necroenzyme radically changed the purpose of the Greenbelt, the Arkhive, and their projects; One of the ingredients of the Necroenzyme is castoreum harvested from Greenbelt Gharials, and are closely guarded by Arkhive's technology.\n\nAnd, well. Resurrecting ancient fauna counts as protecting them, right?",
	["Direct Action"] = "Ever since the Overlay, the business practices on Javion were used a prime example of exploitation of natural resources, as well and especially human resources. Many economic courses use people like Biggs Cradshaw as a figurehead of the sort of person that people should absolutely try their best to avoid becoming, or coming into their town.\nSome people, of course, let examples like those paint their perception of entire corporations, rather than individual people.\nAs a result, movements like the Lordbreakers come to exist in towns, an outlet for people who wish to let out their daily frustrations upon an external culprit to band together and march forward.\n\nTo be fair, their reaction to an enzyme promising eternal life isn't entirely irrational.",
	["Spirit Subpoena"] = "Thec Hiller, better known as the Robloxcity Ripper was a difficult capture for the police. An advanced chemist, his usage of chemicals left no trace of victim, killer, and crime scene; It oftentimes felt like his victims never existed.\nAt the start of the Necroenzyme's introduction to society, many citizens got injected solely to avoid the fate of this serial killer. \n\nBringing him down was an arduous process that required new technology. The best the cops could find in the crime scene were the odd fragments of human remains, nowhere near enough to identify a body...\n\n...Until the NecroForensics Corporation stepped in.\n\n\"You've been invaluable, Margaret. Thanks for telling us who killed you.\"",
	Zoomba = "With the Robloxcity Ripper behind bars, The nefoco turned their attention to more domestic applications of the Enzyme. Robloxians have always feared artifical intelligence beginning with the legends of Chromafex oh so long ago; How do you make sure they'll obey you? How do you make sure they can be stopped?\n\nApollo has put his money and his brain to the solution: Noobs can't destroy the world. Why not just make their intellect Noobish?",
	["Reckless Recruiter"] = "Astarossa Van Buren acted quickly with the production of the necroenzyme, forcing producers to share it and prevent hoarding, scalping, or price gouging. Immortality is a basic right akin to that of water or shelter; It should be free to everyone who wants it, no questions asked.\n\nWith such benevolence, it's not hard to persuade others to vote for him.",
	Disenfranchise = "Of course, a political party requires lackeys. Vice Mayors. Accountants. Advertisers. Public orators. \n\nThe most diehard supporters of the CRP, known among each other as the Astral Faith, believes mortality to be immoral by dragging down healthcare services with your easily preventable illness and disease. Bodily autonomy has led to all sorts of stupid movements that spread disease in the past; Not this time. Besides, making people reliant on what you're selling is good practice in business and politics alike.\n\nSuch underhanded tactics would earn the ire of Astarossa if he knew about them, and they know that. Their subtlety is matched only by their undying faith in Astarossa.",
	["Public Immortality House"] = "The first few enzyme houses secured Astarossa's reelection, with promises of many more to come.\n\nOther mayors of Robloxia's many cities started to take notice of this radical new campaign. With their high demand for the enzyme, coupled with a monopoly on the supply of the Necroenzyme, everyone had to trade with Bloxburg at a premium for their shipments.\n\nBloxburg was about to become very, very rich indeed.",
	["Unerring Temperance"] = "Still, as Astarossa's favourite childhood film said: With great power comes great responsibility.\n\nIt would be easy for all this to get to a leader's head; Greed and pride are pathetic yet potent traps for the weak and unworthy.\n\nThose stupid enough to pursue power for its own sake have no right to wield it. An eternal politician - No. An eternal benevolent philosopher-king, trained in statesmanship, will keep such sycophants at bay.",
	["Defender of Democracy"] = "With the death of Astarossa's brother before his 9th reelection, people urged the Mayor to abandon his nightly walks. It wasn't safe for him to be peacefully strolling around when under such danger. \nAstarossa thinks the smiley familey are nothing more than insecure weaklings masquerading as monsters because they're too pathetic to earn people's respect otherwise. \nIf they want to break his face, prove him right over a simple disagreement, that's their mistake to make.\n\nIt took several arguments for the Astral Faith to talk Astarossa out of what they believe are reckless actions, and he still insisted on his nightly strolls. They couldn't handle their beloved \"prophet\" falling into harm.\n\nHe'll thole the odd bodyguard, though.",
	["Pent-up Pentagenarian"] = "Astarossa's most ardent supporters are the older generations who remember when Bloxburg was little more than a lakeside fishing village. How quickly he changed that! Their lives improved so quickly and so steeply... And they resent the younger generations for not appreciating that further.\n\nAstarossa fixed the economy and turned Bloxburg from a village to a city.\nWith the Necroenzyme dominated by Bloxburg's industries, what will Bloxburg become next? A city-state? A country? The envy of all Robloxia? Or more?",
	["Absolute Authority"] = "In his now-distant youth, Astarossa was a common soldier in the tail end of the Demon Wars. He and many fighting-capable men of his prime age were conscripted by their at-the-time overlord Herrus to fight his battles. It was one giant, country-wide protection racket, and the village of Bloxburg was hardly large enough to object.\n\n50 years later, and demonic supremacy over Robloxia has been abated. No more do they send fighting men to die in trenches on their behalf, and only a tiny handful of revel demons are powerful enough to collect their soul taxes.\nStill, the scars can be felt; many villages lost an entire generation of people, sacrificed for the game of power. What irked Astarossa the most were how larger settlements got light amounts of conscription, owing to their shady deals and influence with Herrus himself. \n\nNow a war veteran-turned-statesman, such nepotism taught Astarossa that the pleas of the weak fall on deaf ears.\nHe will ensure his city is heard.\n\nThus created one of the Necrosyndicates pivotal to Bloxburg's decay.",
	["Hard-hat Immortal"] = "With production of the enzyme in full force, safety concerns across many occupations across Bloxburg rapidly declined, the construction sector being a key example. In order to cut costs and speed up construction with the now growing population of Bloxburg, many companies began cutting back on accident prevention, as a simple dose of enzyme would fix up any work injuries occured. \n\t\t\n\t\tCrissbach and Son's, the previous top bid for many of Bloxburg's large construction projects, was one of the few who refused to reduce safety precautions following the enzyme's distribution, resulting in them to lose top spot in Mayor Astarossa's new developments for his next term.\n\t\t\n\t\t\"We would never disregard the safety of our workers, no matter what magical serum exists. What if they don't want to take it? What if something happens to the supply? It's immoral to rely so heavily on such a thing.\" Said the owner of Crissbach and Son's in a press conference shortly after the Mayor's appointment.",
	["Sig, Street Sweepin Savant"] = "\tThe pedestrian signal glowed dimly red as the display for the hand symbol emerged. Against the night sky, the streetlights above both individuals brighten their figures.\n\nAstarossa and the stranger stared at each other from opposite ends of the crosswalk. There was hardly any traffic at this time of day, they both could cross if they wanted to. Yet they did not. One out of basic decency for the law, the other...for something else. This had been a perfect time for Astarossa to have went on one of his regular nightly strolls. It seemed to be so for the stranger as well, as the smile plastered on his face only grew wider upon making eye contact with the mayor, the stranger's eyes widening for the briefest of moments out of recognition. Astarossa's face remained stoic as ever, though inside he can't quite stamp out the rising feeling of mild surprise as he too now recognizes the stranger. With those ridiculous clothes, how could he not? The pedestrian signal makes the switch over to the walking green human, signaling both parties to proceed. Human. That wasn't quite a word the mayor would use to describe this thing, this visage of a war veteran. Both veterans initiate their pace through the crosswalk, each evenly matched in speed. Neither borne out of malice or hesitation. Astarossa could almost feel the dirt on his hands from those trenches back then, sent there to fight and die on a demon's behalf. Perhaps the thing felt the same way?\n\nNo. Empathy was certainly not a suitable reaction for this situation. This was merely a nightly stroll. That was all.\n\nAs the distance closes, a veil of suppression that encased a memory begins to dissolve. Astarossa stops in place at the sound of a soft splash. …Stop? No, the mayor was still in his stride, but the fledgling of 50 years prior had. They were now within arm’s length of each other, the splashing noises growing in frequency. The weather channel hadn’t called for rain that night, there had been no puddles for the mayor to navigate around.\n\nAh, of course. That made sense.\n\nThe thing begins to raise his hand. No fear wells up with Astarossa, but that did not mean he was to be oblivious as he watches the thing out of the corner of his eye as they start to pass each other. And yet… The thing tips his hat at Astarossa with a gloved left hand. The very hand that gripped the mayor’s own from way back then. The mayor gives his own hat tip in response. It was only polite, if nothing else. A remnant of the revel army did not need much more. Astarossa was now on the other side of the street. He was sure the thing was staring at his back, but his stride continues nonetheless. There was no need to entertain the thing any further. \n\nThe pedestrian signal glowed dimly red as the display for the hand symbol emerged once more. \n",
	Rapport = "“Cya, Mr. Nalrad!”\n“Come visit Povvo Street sometime! Bet you and Harry’ll get along great!”\nWith a spring in their step, both teenagers start making their way out of the Greenbelt back towards Bloxburg, minds newly armed with war stories and techniques of slaughter. A soft smile is etched across Sig’s face as he looks upon the fading figures of the troubled, yet determined kids. That determination is always great to see in those that exude it.\nThat is why he simply can’t just shackle himself down to one place, one group. For he wished to guide all those that needed it towards the star in their lives. It did not matter who, for seeing those he blesses work towards their ambitions and dreams with his assistance was enough for him.\n\nSig looked down at the mask the teenagers had given him. It was flattering, tempting even. Perhaps if he were what he once ‘was’ back then…\nHe shakes his head. The fledgling soldier of many decades past had already passed on. This is who he was now.\n\n“Sorry, kiddos. It’s gonna be a no from me.”\nSig gently places the mask down leaning against the log he had been sitting on as to not damage it, and begins making his own way back towards Bloxburg.",
	["Laughing Stock"] = "Abandoned in Bloxburg's slums, six child orphans of the Demon Wars banded together in a bloody protection pact; An attack on one of them is an attack on them all that will be met with bloody retribution. The boys matured, and so had their skills. The strongest of them had elevated such defensive brutality into an artform, turning their protection pact into the largest and most feared gang in Bloxburg and its neighbours. When turning to organised crime, many people get corrupted by the power and the evils used to sustain it. Not the smileys; The elders of the crime gang know full well how poor their lives were before joining the family, steering those from more affluent backgrounds away from their hedonistic lifestyles and into the Smiley values of honesty, gratitude, and family. The result is a strongly-knit community tied together not by blood, but by family all the same. No matter how terrible your life is, how much pain you're in, how much the world scorns you, remember to smile.",
	["Chuckling Arsonist"] = "The smileys live life by a simple premise: The familey is the most important thing. Leave the familey alone, and it'll leave you alone too. Their predictability is why Astarossa has permitted their existence for so long; They won't bother people if they're not bothered. As the old saying goes, let sleeping dogs lie. It's a shame bloxburg at large refuses to learn that fact.",
	["Snickering Skewer"] = "The most dangerous of the Smiley's opponents as they fought for supremacy over Bloxburg's narcotics routes were the Skewerglee Gang. Half inspired by the Smiley's own hardcore code of conduct - and the punishments that break them - their territory were marked by pikes, decorated with their opponents.\nKingrin saw this breakaway sect as an attack on the familey's values. As overtly selfish, putting their needs before the needs of the familey.\nThe battle between the two gangs lasted two months, with Povvo Street painted red with their blood. It took such waste of a family for the losers to throw down their arms and rejoin the group.\nThose that did were welcomed with open arms.",
	["Carnage Crowd"] = "Still, a diehard group of Skewerglees refused to ingratiate themselves back into the Smileys, citing how stifled they felt by the familey's rules. Did they have to wear these masks so often?\nKingrin, a father figure to this newer generation of smileys, laughed at them. Boys will be boys. He would've let them walk, let them find freedom in their own terms.\nThen they insulted the masks.",
	["Cackling Hell Biker"] = "Astarossa's brother was repeatedly warned not to antagonise the Smileys, and rejected the mayor's pleas to reconsider.\nThe brother, Alexander-Pfeffel Van Buren, had enough of this gang befoulling this city, making it impossible for them to develop that blight Povvo Street into a nice high-rise real estate.\nHe went into Povvo street and demanded to meet the leader of the Smileys.\nIf some Smiley tried to run him over, he's the Mayor's brother. You don't want to anger Astarossa, right?",
	["Animal Experimentation Kit"] = "A master surgeon in her dayjob, Fl00fy_Bonez has manipulated and twisted the Necroenzyme for her own ends. Using the regenerative abilities of the enzyme, she has stitched together cat ears and other cute accessories for herself and her rave followers. In addition to the accessories, she also performs a minor lobotomy on her new recruits, dulling their pain senses and making them far happier.\nBeing your authentic self has never been so easy or fun!\nIt's fine. Animals can't feel pain, and they're great at alleviating the pain of others.",
	["Raving Rascal"] = "The PLURRAL roam around the PLURRALITY, a nightclub that has been subjected to several noise ordinances.\nHere, people drown away their sorrow with music, drinks, dancing, and more. The music is so loud, the lights so dazzling, that the odd accident that inevitably happens is passed up as a joke.\nWhat's a crowd crush between immortal friends?",
	["Pawesome Party"] = "The mindless thrill-seeking of the PLURRALs earn them the contempt of the few that know of their secret underground nightclub. After going through the process of being \"unburdened,\" many of those surgically altered by Floofy_Bonez are unable to return to their now-sickened families.\nIn wanting to belong, they return back to the PLURRALITY, where they can party the night away.",
	["Excited Bouncer"] = "While the PLURRALITY is open to everyone, those who are still \"burdened\" - unaltered by Fl00fy_Bonez - Are pitied. Don't you want to be free of pain? Don't you want to be happy?\nA few of the burdened share their pity and are waiting for the appropriate time to be their authentic self. Between celebrities, clergymen, and members of the Mayor's inner circle, many don't have the time for their appointment... Yet.\nSome unburdened dislike being called such, and lash out in the PLURRALITY. Those people are quickly shown the door.",
	["Last Dance Hedonist"] = "Despite how much transfiguration Sarah did on the hospital's past patients, some of them were far too gone to be made more 'healthy'.\nNothing to worry about, though. Everything'll be fine! On to the others!",
	["Tempted by Redemption"] = "It hurt. It hurt too much.\nShe looked at herself in the mirror. She looked like a wreck.\nIt was supposed to help them! It was supposed to make them feel better!\nIt was supposed to help her! It was supposed to make her feel better!\nWhy didn't it work? Why didn't it help?\nIt's been five months. It's been so long.\nShe hated it. She hated this.\nMaybe...\nMaybe she can just make it go away...",
	["Sarah Greene Bailey"] = "-Testimony by Dr. Grey- -cont.-\n-...-Look. All in all, she was a great doctor, and I really would've trusted her with a lot.\nShe had a thing with emotions, could read other people quite well. Made lots of younger patients happier just by being around too, thanks to her enthusiasm. Helped alot with making prep for surgeries, especially high risk ones.\nBluntly speaking though, and as much as it hurts to state it now of all times, she was never the best at introspection.",
	["Counsel Engine"] = "--INTERMISSION--\nThe loss of Alexa Neinstein was a great loss to the scientific and magical community. The inventor of the entanglement drive, she opened the floodgates for so-called magiscientists to explore the workings of the particles inside of studs themselves.\nNaturally, she donated her body to science. It's what any self-respecting scientist does.\nNow she can use her overwhelming intellect for whatever breakthrough the highest seller wants. The mayor and military are especially interested...",
	["Bloxburg Messiah Hospital"] = "A triad formed to help those in need after the Overlay, now a large hospital district situated near the Bloxburg Greenbelt. Bloxburg Messiah Hospital acts as a semi-charity organization dedicated to providing affordable healthcare to those in need.\nEver since the rise of the Necrosyndicates, the same hospital district is currently used a place of refuge for those wishing to stay safe during the conflict occuring at the main city.\nSurely, no one's going to be interested in a place which doesn't store any trace of the necroenzyme, right?",
	["Illusion of Failure"] = "...the low, droning sound of a flatline is dreadful to listen to.\n\t\tAt least the forest's nearby...",
	["Say Goodbyes"] = "--INTERMISSION--\nThe most popular of the NecroForensic Corporation's products is the Halogenic Aerosol. By dispersing a small dose of the necroenzyme across a wide area, police are able to interrogate mass murders, resurrect entire ecosystems, as well as put on dazzling bug displays.\nThe Halogenic Aerosol has civil applications, too. It allows the NeFoCo to reanimate many lost people for a short while, allowing them to consent to zombification and continue life, or allow their families the ability to properly mourn their passing.\nEveryone deserves to be able to say goodbye.",
	["Observation Cam"] = "Naturally, so much enzyme in the middle of nowhere is a great target for thieves. Caitlyn can't stop them stealing it, but she can stop them leaving the forest once they do.",
	["Hive Terminal"] = "The Greenbelt is an expansive stretch of forestry that takes five hours to drive from one end to the other. So to monitor would-be poachers and communicate with each other, the Arkhive has set up multiple communication pylons.\nTheir self-defence systems make the Arkhive blush.",
	["Fauna Feeding"] = "Besides archaeological work, Arkhive also collaborates with the forest's ranger groups in protecting and taking care of the local wildlife.\nOf course, being situated near a wellspring of pure vitality, most of the fauna are quite well-built. That also means they have a large appetite.",
	["Scripture Scanner"] = "In sector 45-G of the Greenbelt, there exists the ruins of an Alar outpost in prestine condition. The ruins are covered in rubber tyre during the summer to ensure that the humidity doesn't disturb the rock formation, and are researched and respected by the Arkhive in the winter.\nThe Necroenzyme has enhanced the ability to study noobkind's ancestors; The Alar writing system was undecipherable until a local knight buried at the outpost millennia ago was revived. They told the Arkhive about the many outposts scattered around the area as the Alars attempted to fight against the Nevermore Squadron of old. The time of Shedletsky, the Nightmares, and the Draconic Uprising was barely understood during the days of the Necrosyndicates; to have a living account of that timeframe was incalculably helpful for scholars of this time period.\nIt also attracted the Arkhive unwanted attention.",
	["Defiant March"] = "Having gone through likes of the Ragebornes, Javion swindlers and mad Federation elites high on conquest, it's no wonder a lot of citizens have acted more banded together than ever.\nThey've been through far worse than an immortality serum spreading around. ",
	["Katharan Rebuilder"] = "Coming from next to nothing, the Javionese diaspora were put into Povvo Streeet, the cheapest housing. They didn't love the Smileys, but there was a strange kinship between the two. They understood that they just wanted their culture, their families, left alone without outside forces telling them what to do.\nSo when the smileys evacuated a building they were squatting, it was easy to patch it up.",
	["Citizen's Militia"] = "Of all the necrosyndicates, the Lordbreakers have the most animosity with, suprisingly, the NeFoCo. For their mutual hatred of each other, Mckayla and the Mayor had a preverse respect for the other sticking to their principles, no matter what. Immortality is terrible, but Mckayla could believe that scoundrel having the best possible intentions to pave the road to hell with.\nThey can't say the same for the NeFoCo, who the lordbreakers see as powerhungry and exploitative.\nIndeed, despite the animosity the Lordbreakers have towards the undead, many of them have joined to stop their further creation.",
	["Changing Times"] = "The first time Mckayla publicly denounced Astarossa for failing to clean up and shelter the poor was 7 years ago, shortly after the arrival of her and her parents in the city. They were late arrivals, refugees from the Overlay.\nAstarossa spent a lot of time pondering these new people under his care. They were quite different to the people he grew up with; More concerned with rights than work, yet... They cared for each other. Stuck with each other. \nThere's something to admire in that solidarity, even if they repeatedly antagonise him and his work.",
	["Welcome to Bloxburg!"] = "And with that, the stage is set.\nJoin us on March 3rd for Necrosyndicates act 1:",
	["Fashionable Citizen"] = "While Bloxburg will always be remembered for its extreme peculiarities, it is easy to forget that it was a normal city.\nIf the horrors of the Necrosyndicates could happen here, it could happen anywhere.",
	["Empty House"] = "With no one around, the Dwit residence eventually fell into decay.\nIt wasn't filled with much life to begin with.",
	["Neverending Longing"] = "It was filled with pain.",
	["Bioblade Digger"] = "Ever since the Robloxian Overlay, several notable landmarks of Old Robloxia had to bear the brunt of the array of Javion architecture being placed around them. The landmark which took the biggest brunt was The Heights, the most popular swordfighting and tourist spot of the time. The swords which served as the staple of the lands were lost to the grounds, along with their spawn blocks. At first, it seemed impossible for the artifacts to be recovered.\nThat is, until word spread about what happened to The Heights after the Overlay.\nPlanets outside of the Vecross system caught wind of the Overlay ever since a green zillygastian spoke about his experiences and what he saw. Obviously, such a thing would let the connection of dots that something must've happened to The Heights as well. With how notable and popular the spot is for culturists, sparrers and historians outside the Vecross System, it wouldn't be until long until a bunch of species got together to investigate.\nLanding on New Robloxia after an agreement with The Authority of The Heights, several extraterrestrial species began their work on possibly recovering the swords lost to cataclysm, in hopes for fame, glory, or even power.\nTheir expedition name? The Bioblades.",
	["Bioblade Excavator"] = "Digging into the ruins of the Heights can be a bit jarring at first, with the ground being divided into stud parts rather than normally breaking apart into fractured pieces.\nNot much of a problem for the Rivinnes, though. They're used to being intangible.",
	["Bioblade Stud Curator"] = "In recent times, the study of Studs is seen as incredibly basic in the fields of science, akin to noble gases, reactions, and other baseline studies.\nOtherwordly beings, however, find them incredibly interesting, noting their constant universal size with little to no variation.",
	["Bioblade Demolitionist"] = "With the Heights destroyed to the point where it looked like a wasteland, The Authority of The Heights wanted to recover the lost swords before they sought to rebuild the arena from the ground up. Any further destruction on the remains were allowed (as long as it doesn't damage the blades.)\nWho better to call to throw explosives around than the strangely demolition-savant Cruizictants?",
	["Bioblade Chef"] = "Many species got together to collaborate on the expedition, though a good number of them act less as actual excavators and more like supporters.\nThe quiet race of Yelizziavens-Gekis vocalize theirs through food.",
	["Bioblade Supply Manager"] = "With how much distance from Robloxia needs to be covered for each species, supply lines can be an arduous task to make efficient.\nThe Zulajians were more than happy to assist with their atom-based transport systems.",
	["Bioblade Investor"] = "Of course, with the need for supplies comes the need for funding. Can't upheave the ruins of a bunch of tall mountains without the proper green.\nThe bureaucratic Charillits agree, and they expect the proper green to be repaid by what lies within those ruins.",
	["Endless Ice Smasher"] = "Out of any anomalies, a change in temperature is the most noticable in the heat of the Heights.",
	["American Splendor"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 4\n\t\t\"As noticed from the previous blades appraised so far, the shapes bear no resemblance to the swords that the Heights are famous for.\n\t\tOne can assume that the blades found so far were a byproduct of the Overlay, possibly caused by the mass conflux of energies being in close proxity of one another. The generation of these blades may be linked to the blade-regenerating blocks of the Heights previous.\n\t\tThis one in particular - dubbed the American Splendor - may be related to the nationalistic figure previously spotted during the Alpha Brick Heist Incident, bearing an equal level of pure, nationalistic pride within the steel.\"",
	["Heights Expedition Site"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Writer's Note\n\"As per an agreement with the Bioblades and The Heights Authority, I have been commissioned to write a detailed log citing the findings of the Heights Expedition Project. In this book, you will be debriefed about the discoveries and observations made by the Bioblades, explained through personal interpretations.\nThe creation of this book is stemmed from scientific and cultural interest into the Robloxian Overlay. Due to this, certain details of the swords found will be redacted in order to preserve regional and military secrecy, as per requested by The Heights Authority.\nDenoted,\nXhartyr\"",
	["Grand Ivory"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 5\n\t\t\"The Grand Ivory - a sword with clear religious markings, bearing the obvious connection to warriors of the Heavens.\n\t\tSuch in mind, it is clear this sword is related to the Guardias, an ancient civilization of paladins who hailed from the skies.\"",
	["Shattered Earth"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 6\n\t\t\"The Shattered Earth. It leaves little to no question what caused this sword to form.\n\t\tLogs of ancient tectonic beasts who formed themselves after the ground they eventually became were catalogued long ago. With the absolute destruction of the Heights, perhaps a little of their wrath was incited and used in the forming this blade.\"",
	["Twisted Onyx"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 7\n\t\t\"The Twisted Onyx - a blade so jagged, it ends up being less efficient than other swords when it comes to actually cutting.\n\t\tOnly a madman would think to use this blade. In that same regard, that same madman would be able to use this sword to its fullest potential.\"",
	["Shameless Scimitar"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 8\n\t\t\"The Shameless Scimitar.\n\t\tThe rest of the expedition team are beginning to think the Heights are sentient.\n\t\tIf that were so, they have a certain sense of comedy.”",
	["Celtic Blade"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 9\n\t\"The Celtic Blade. Imagery chiseled on the sword is local to the Huntlands, a neighbouring country to the Heights.\n\tThe sword seems to boost the natural fortune of those who wield it, as the tradition is stated in the Huntlands.\n\tNowadays, they've been assigning one member of each expedition to carry it around whenever they wanted to dig, meant to both assist in finding more blades as well as morale.\"",
	["Infernal Undead"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 10\n\t\"The Infernal Immortal, a nod to the undead and the practice of necromancy.\n\tThe vitalic essence that emanates from this sword is corrupting. Wielders have felt their hands begin to tremble out of their own accord.\n\tSymbolism from this sword and source does not seem to be obvious. Perhaps it could pertain to the Overseers and their rituals in order to transcend death itself.\n\tOnly one can tell.\"",
	["Gingerbread Sword"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 11\n\t\"The Gingerbread Sword. Made of purely condensed sugar and baked well enough to serve as a solid blade.\n\tConfectionaries are a widespread field, even outside of New Robloxia - even Old Robloxia, so using that as the defined factor of the formation of this blade may be pure speculation.\n\tPerhaps it may be related to the Yelizziavens-Gekis who joined on the expedition. Desserts are a dish served to the excavators afterhours.\"",
	["Frightful Blade of Bone"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 12\n\t\"The Frightful Blade of Bone - carved out of skull parts and held together by bolts.\n\tOne can assume this sword is linked to the massacres that occured during the Alpha Wars, leading to the deaths of billions.\"",
	["Wicked-Heart"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 13\n\t\"The Wicked-Heart. A symbol of cruelty.\n\tRegulated swordfighting is controlled as to make sure grevious injury is avoided. In war, however, records of inhumane torture through the use of blades are noted by the hundreds.\n\tWe can only take gratitude in the fact we may never come to another war in the near future.\"",
	["The Heartshaker"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 14\n\t\"The Heartshaker - a blade with obvious love-related motifs.\n\tThe creation of this sword may be linked to the group known as the Slenders, often commonly referred to as ODers - engaging in dating in an almost excessive amount.\"",
	["Future Falchion"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 15\n\t\"The Future Falchion - a blade made of vibranium and fitted with alpha ray emitters capable enough of ionizing particles to the point where it'd form a searing cut.\n\tThe blade itself is lightweight, allowing easy wielding with a single-handed style.\n\tFor the source of formation, it may be linked to the rapid advancements in technology that had been occuring in the late Vecross System prior to the Federation Conquests.\"",
	["Venom's Bite"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 16\n\t\"The Venom's Bite - a blade brimming with poison.\n\tIn order to wield it, the user must have already developed an immunity to basic poisons beforehand to avoid any adverse effects.\n\tThe catalyst for this blade's formation may be linked to the recently discovered Vitality Wellspring. It may be depicting the less graceful fact about the Wellspring, being its dependancy on the cycle of death and decay in order to properly infuse more vitalic essence into its waters.\"",
	["Vlad's Lament"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 17\n\t\t\"The Vlad's Lament - a blade that attracts the blood from the wounds of its victims.\n\t\tThe best wielder for this blade is one which does not fear losing blood themselves, as the blade's attraction is indiscriminate.\n\t\t\tThe source of its formation is peculiar, being linked to a popular horror species known as Vampires, with their most popular depiction being Count Vlad Dracula Tepes. The reason for this species in particular to be used as a catalyst is unknown.\"",
	["Burning Embrace"] = "-The Lost Swords of the Heights - Found- by Xhartyr, Page 18\n\t\t\t\t\"The Burning Embrace - an iron blade encasing solid volcanic essence in its core, keeping it in a constant, searing temperature while keeping the handle safe.\n\t\t\t\tThe vortexes of fire which appear around the Heights seem to be its closest source, with an obvious correlation between their fiery natures.\"",
	["Sacred Chaos Blade"] = "-Personal Diary of Xhartyr- - An Excerpt\n\t\t\t\t\"The thoughts of what I have seen eats away at me at night.\n\t\t\t\tI may never be able to tell the tale to another living soul, nor will I find myself having closure from such a thing.\n\t\t\t\tWith this, I hope to atleast ease my own mind, through materialization of my experience.\n\t\t\t\tIt was empty, nothing. I walked upon a pool of the void.\n\t\t\t\tBodies laid there, motionless, expressionless. Not dead, but unresponsive.\n\t\t\t\tI looked upon the sky. I saw the blades that the Heights prided themselves over.\n\t\t\t\tThey shined under the light of the vortex.\n\t\t\t\tThey were unified.\n\t\t\t\tAnd so too were the reflections of the bodies.\"",
	["Xhartyr - Bladescribe"] = "\"It stares down at me, like a predator to its prey.\"\n\"I could feel its gaze everywhere from where I stood. Even till now.\"\n\"Yet, knowing that thing originated from the land of swordsmanship. A land of strife.\"\n\"I needed only one response.\"\n\"To fight.\"",
	["Sleepless Steward"] = "Hazenwyld, 426 AD.\nTwenty years have passed since the Overlay that fused Javion and Robloxia together.\nEclipse is back in peaceful solitude, his lunar prison orbiting New Robloxia.\nThe Overlay ended the Rageborne crisis, leaving everyone involved happy yet damaged.\n- The Katharan, Havaluvian, Forothians, having all fled to Javion, only to again flee to Robloxia, finally know peace.\n- The Paraselene Sages, which protect the universe from Powered threats, Lost a traitorous Evincar, but gained a more powerful loyal one.\n- The plans of Adreti and his prime Rageborne cohorts to inflict mass misery on Javion to turn everyone Rageborne was foiled, and their progeny have been uplifted with the kind philosophies of Yuéliáng and Hóu Yi.\nOf all the remainders of the Vecross system, it is the Cothrite Diaspora, separated from their home planet, that have suffered the most.\nBecause they were the first target of Adreti's schemes.",
	["Extruded Gentleman"] = "After the Overlay, a new existence emerged between the Rageborne and the people they inhabit, known as a vassal. Two completely separate, intelligent, independent people, inhabiting the same body, transforming via sleep.\nFor while they are indeed borne from a feral state, Ragebornes mellow out with time, becoming a kind, gentle people.\nHow this bond, this gestalt between rageborne and vassal is handled with is a deeply personal matter. Yuéliáng and Hóu Yi saw each other as work colleagues, Although she wished it could be more at the end, the two were stalwart, platonic friends.\nSome gestalts hate each other. Some gestalts are friends.\nBut for some, the bond between two souls sharing a body is unbreakably strong.",
	["Extruded Lady"] = "Being married to yourself is hardly strange in Hazenwyld, the Rageborne Sanctum.",
	["Cothrite Shepherd"] = "Zanzel looked at what her people had become in disgust. The proud people of Cothran, who challenged the planet-conquering Federation, reduced to beggars and vagabonds. The same people who took her in with open arms as a child, now wary of her untainted presence as an adult.\nLocked away from their ancestral home, unable to commune with their spirits, ravaged by Adreti to be full of Ragebornes, the Cothrite Diaspora struggled with their identity. Their culture was communing with their ancestral spirits for counsel, yet only one spirit wished to answer: Their rageborne.\nFor what is a rageborne if not a spirit inside you? What is a vassal if not a container for other people?\nZanzel scoffed at the symmetry between her pristine faith and this perversion. She originally respected Pangu's leadership, the archpriest of Cothran appointed by her deeply beloved uncle Ptenda. But if he insists on being the plaything of that monstrous Chiyou, she would insist on preserving the Cothrite faith.\nStarting by saving the \"vassals\" from being slaves to other people.",
	["Yang-Chiyou, Sword of Cothran"] = "Once again, Wa-Pangu woke up with a broken arm and fresh scars drizzled across his body. How many times had his bed, a mottled mess of straw and blankets, had to see him endure this pain? Although reprimanding his rageborne made the damage to his body far less than in the early days, he'd still like it if he didn't wake up in this state at all; His age wasn't doing him any favours.\nLurching to the side of the bed, Pangu once again tried to commune with the spirits in his body. While the crisis days of the Overlay were long behind us, while the Cothrite diaspora was in relative calm, it was his duty as an archpriest to gather the counsel of his ancestors.\nSilence.\nAnother signal sent out for communication.\nSilence.\nNo, this would not do. The purpose of Cothrite's ancestors are to serve their progeny. Once again, Pangu sent a signal through his body louder than his throbbing headache, demanding a conversation.\nOnce again, silence, followed by a frustrated sigh.\nOf all 300 spirits in his body, only one was receptive to conversation and it was the last one Pangu wished to commune with.\nFine. \nPangu lifted his broken arm and vigorously stretched, melting it down into a mess of black and red glass. This glass pulled itself out of Pangu's body, assembling into a thick, muscular arm, followed by a rippling, scar-drizzled chest, followed by hulking legs and feet. The brute's head was the last part to be extruded out, a tangled mess of teeth and thorns, now smiling at Pangu.\nEven by the standards of Rageborne, Pangu's was a towering monster, well over three times his size. Yet the brute still felt the pain of the broken arm the two of them shared, collapsing onto Pangu, pinning him onto the bed. Pangu was scooped up into his arms for a warm hug with a wink and a smile.\n\"Ey, princess. What's the beef?\"\nDespite all his grievances, Pangu couldn't help but cradle him back.",
	["Umwelt Shift"] = "Pangu looked at Chiyou dead in his sharp red eyes.\n\"The 'beef,'\" Pangu explained in the same way a parent would lecture a child, \"is that I asked you to stop getting into fights and leaving me to deal with the damage.\"\nChiyou whined.\n\"Yeah, I'm sorry. But that Zanzel git, y'know? Going around saying we're 'parasites' and a drain on our hosts. Can't stand 'er.\"\nPangu rubbed the broken arm the two of them shared.\n\"She is of that opinion because of how you you treat me. She does not like seeing her godfather in pain.\"\n\"Nah, she's just a twat. That and how ya can't communicate with yer spirits anymore, princess. 'e thinks she's better than ya.\"\nAn offended Pangu clamped his mouth shut.\n\"I cannot communicate with them because of how rambuctious you are. They are scared of you.\"\n\"Nah, princess! They've abandoned you! Abandoned us! They don't like what we've got going! They don't like us little Rageborne, trying to make a living in a new world hostile to our existence!\" \nChiyou's shouting echoed around the room, reverberating off the walls. Pangu braced himself for a confrontation as Chiyou flailed his arms in frustration.#\nBut, as vassal and rageborne often do, the two looked at each other, shared their bodies and minds with each other, felt the other's feelings.\nPangu's fear at his abandonment by his ancestors. How he can't talk to them, and thus can't do his duties as archpriest.\nChiyou's fear of his Rageborne brethren being cast out. That Zanzel might do something bad to them. That he'll have to protect them.\nThese sudden rushes of empathy were never predictable, but always welcomed. Their trance lasted moments but felt like hours of learning, understanding, being the other, seeing the world in their eyes in impossible detail. \nThe two laughed at each other. Laughed with each other. \nDespite their incessant bickering, the two cared for each other fondly.",
	["Ying-Pangu, Shield of Cothran"] = "\"...Look, princess,\" Chiyou laid down on the bed beside Pangu. \n\"When I was but a knave, you saved me from a life of villainy and depravity. Without ya tracking down that Yueliang lass, I would simply not be a person. Most of us wouldn't.\"\nChiyou's face let forth a dribbling of happy, blissful tears. \"I know yer set in yer ways trying to be the hero Cothran wants you to be. But you are a rageborne hero too. We love ya, and it hurts to see ya ignore that love for a people that don't love ya back.\"\nPangu sat contentedly. Every day he would ask himself what he was; Can you be Cothrite if the spirits don't listen to you? Can you be Cothrite so far away from your home planet? Can you be Cothrite if you have a loud yet wholesome monster ranting on about chivalry inside you? Pangu smiled in his realisation that he had spent so long debating if he was truly Cothrite that he forgot how irrelevant the question was.\n\"So don't worry, princess. I know those ancestors have abandoned ya, but I never will! I'm yer knight in shining armour!\"\nPangu appreciated the sentiment but could not hold back a groan. Chiyou smirked at Pangu's cringing.\nPangu had made his mind up; It was time for his old age and old ideas to retire. Pass the mantle of Cothrite Archpriest to Zanzel if she cares the old ways so much. But that could wait.\nHe opened a drawer besides the bed, and procured a TV remote. The next episode of Detective Scott was about to air.\nWhat better way to spend time with your soulmate?",
	["Comforting Words"] = "...You're a strong person.\nI'm... sure you can help others if you keep that spirit of yours up.\nJust do what your heart truly believes in.\nLosing both of his parents and his legs in the span of a single night, the child was devastated.\nA nurse's empathetic advice was the only thing that saved him from a life of continous regret.",
	["Protracted Murder"] = "One year has passed since Eisenhower Dwit invented the Necroenzyme. Now fully entrenched within the society of Bloxburg, its effects are deeply felt by all of its residents.\nWith the Enzyme allowing incredible regeneration and reanimation from even tiny fractions of bodies, traditional methods of murder and death have been rendered useless.\nSo the city's underworld naturally got to work inventing new ways of silencing those they dislike. With the immortal reliant on the enzyme, the city's underworld took a more brutal tone, relying on stealthy kidnapping and detainment over fast and easy headshots or stabbings. Once the target is in a secure location, put them in a place they can't escape from and starve them to death.\nImmortality doesn't stop you from dying; It stops your death from being boring.",
	["Paraselene Starsleuth"] = "With such spectacular events surrounding Bloxburg and its syndicates, the world is watching the sleepy city with ceaseless attention. The city of bloxburg and its Enzyme trade are an ever-evolving landscape, changing daily as Astarossa passes new rules, people jockey for the NeFoCo's enzyme production, and the Arkhive raise more and more security on the precious ingredients needed to make the Enzyme.\nThe necrosyndicates must be quick to adapt in such an unknown world.",
	["Crackdown Enforcer"] = "Astarossa endorsed the Enzyme because it would enable him to provide a better healthcare service for his citizens, as well as keep his diehard yet aging voterbase in power without subverting democracy.\nYet with the enzyme flowing unrestricted and people using it for all sorts of fabulous and nefarious deeds, the flow of Enzyme for its proper, intended use - ensuring citizens have a high quality of healthcare - has been stymied.\nIt was the Smileys raiding a hospital for more Enzyme to sell that caused Astarossa to sever his backend deals with them. The Smileys are no longer useful idiots for his platform, instead being scapegoats his voters are bloodthirsty to see justice to.\nIt's time to clean up the streets.",
	["Smiley Spawn"] = "The one code of the Smileys are simple: Leave them alone, and they'll leave you alone in too.\nTurning down gout treatment for a kid because of his familey? That's just discrimination.\nIf Astarossa is going to renege on their deal, so will they. And oh, how that bastard will suffer so much worse than his brother did.\nAllowances aren't cheap, y'know.",
	["Hunting Party"] = "As part of their efforts to eradicate pain and suffering, the PLURRAL harvest animals from Bloxburg's greenbelt, fusing them with their bodies to make them their Authentic Selves.\nYou may think that harvesting animals for their skin makes you a monster. This is something only Burdened people, ones that need to be liberated from their pain, would say. Just look at Caitlin and how much weight she carries, being a robot and resurrecting the dead to record their irrelevant, unfun history.\nShe'd be so much happier with cat ears on her.",
	["Extant Anomalocaris"] = "With the increasing attacks on Bloxburg's Greenbelt for animal parts and Enzyme, Caitlin has sent most of the Arkhive away for their safety.\nIf these chodes want her, her enzyme, and her pussies so badly, they can come an' get 'er.\nWith nothing but her own wits, her bike and axe, and the largest stash of the Enzyme after the NeFoCo The Paladin of Nature will defend the forest on her own, but hardly alone.",
	["Zoomba Rebel"] = "The Javionese tell horror stories about their old ruler, Biggs. A callous, immortal lich who controlled the flow of the planet's magic money to sustain his immortality, most of the Javionese diaspora are happy Yueliang destroyed Javion, as it means they are free of him... For now.\nThe Lordbreakers have vowed to never allow such a force of evil have reign over them again, which is exactly what this Enzyme could allow.\nPragmatists, the Lordbreakers don't see the NeFoCo as enemies, per se; McKayla even admires how Apollo crawled himself out of extreme adversity to the position he is today. But with that loathesome xenophobe Thec loose, aiming for Apollo's throat, the NeFoCo are distracted, and thus are easy targets to end this immortal madness.\nAnd there are many who want the NeFoCo to end.",
	["Mass Production"] = "With Apollo distracted handling the defence of the NeFoCo to keep the city's Enzyme supply running, the more avaricious members of the board of directors took control of day to day operations.\nThe Lordbreakers may smash their supply, but at what cost to them? To the NeFoCo? To the city? Push too far, and severing the entire supply may have dire consequences.\nFor now, though, the enzyme flows freely.",
	["Enzymic Citizen"] = "Finally, the citizens of Bloxburg go about their daily lives. Life has been a bit hard with the syndicates, but any drastic change to a society will have its fair share to kinks to sort out.\nImmortality's worth it, right?",
	["Polluted Vitality Wellspring"] = "Finally, because you've been paying attention, one last teaser:\nOne of the ingredients of the Enzyme is water from Bloxburg's Wellspring, a supposed fountain of youth the original village was based around. Given how important it is to the Enzyme, it seems there were truth to the rumours.\nBut with the enzyme being mass produced, the fountain is starting to dry up.\nWhat will become of Bloxburg's most famous location then?",
	["Prep for Survival"] = "Caitlin managed to outrun the PLURRAL, but she knows an altercation against them will occur again. Heavily outnumbered, she had to figure out a way to even out the odds.\nWith a reluctant digital sigh, she prepped up supplies at the supply shack and headed out towards Greenbelt's Tomb of the Unknown Armies.",
	["Astral Faith Evangelist"] = "Astarossa sat in his office, mulling over a detailed report placed on his desk.\nThe issue had come to his knowledge since a month ago. Rumours of a shadow organization brewing within the Committee for Rational Progress adopting medieval ideals were spread silently, with a faithful bodyguard being Astarossa's informant.\nRemoving this tumor from the town hall is mandatory, but doing so would need the effort to occur in as quick as a process as possible in order to send a message towards those who wish to proselytize the Necroenzyme.\nThe kickstart for such an effort to begin planning came from an ex-member of the Astral Faith coming forth with a fearful, but brave whistleblow.\nThe gruesome, sickening details only invigorated Astarossa's desire to bring down the Faith.",
	["Astral Faith Zealot"] = "Astarossa sat in his office, mulling over a detailed report placed on his desk.\nThe issue had come to his knowledge since a month ago. Rumours of a shadow organization brewing within the Committee for Rational Progress adopting medieval ideals were spread silently, with a faithful bodyguard being Astarossa's informant.\nRemoving this tumor from the town hall is mandatory, but doing so would need the effort to occur in as quick as a process as possible in order to send a message towards those who wish to proselytize the Necroenzyme.\nThe kickstart for such an effort to begin planning came from an ex-member of the Astral Faith coming forth with a fearful, but brave whistleblow.\nThe gruesome, sickening details only invigorated Astarossa's desire to bring down the Faith.\n",
	["Egregious Entryism"] = "\"...the sole fact the Necroenzyme came from our fauna is a sign that we are destined for greatness, to become as one with the deities of this world!\"\n\"Those who seek to cling onto their mortality are fools! They forgo a path to a higher apex!\"\n\"Which is why we must---\"\nSMASH!!\n\"...what the...?\"",
	["Schism in the Party"] = "The takedown of the Astral Faith was efficient and straightforward.\nAstarossa stated his intentions and demands to the boastful zealot, giving an opportunity for them to forgo the option of violence.\nWhen they did pick that option, however, Astarossa simply took off his hat and put on a pair of iron knuckles.\nIt's been a long while since those CQC techniques were useful.",
	["Torturing Turncoat"] = "Somewhere, in a dimly lit basement, an Evangelist stays chained to the wall.\nHe sits there, exasperated. This would be the 11th time he had experienced death.\nHis captor enters from the nearby staircase. Seeing him prep a drill, the Evangelist had decided to give up.\nThrough a tired gasp, the captive talked. Details about the Bloxburg Town Hall were shared. Entrances, exits, weaknesses, defenses.\nThe torturer had gotten the information that his familey needed.",
	["Biggs, Liquidated"] = "\"Hey, hey, Bigg Spenders! It's your Top B, Biggs Cradshaw on AIR! Been a good twenty-one years, hasn't it? Well, you'll sure be happy to know your sigma-delta-hyperion guy is still alive and kickin'!\nSure, I may have been abandoned by the galaxy's greatest bouncer and my co-businessman, but who needs them? The grind keeps going!\nI've recently gotten into contact with some TOP executives of a familiar company that's about 'charity' and whatever lame buzz words synonomous with that! Through them, I've gotten a little taste of B-B-Bloxburg's latest craze! Lemme tell ya, Bigg Spenders, this'll be my BIGG BREAK! Just you wait and see!\"",
	["Eternal Justice Mk.2"] = "As the Lordbreakers began their raid on the NeFoCo Headquarters, Apollo activated the defense protocols in order to protect the supplies inside the company's warehouses. These defense protocols were designed to ensure that control of the headquarters would be secured through non-lethal methods.\nWhile the company's human workers followed Apollo's regulations in non-lethal control, the automated machines, however, were provided a different protocol.",
	["Organoid “Officer"] = "As the Lordbreakers began their raid on the NeFoCo Headquarters, Apollo activated the defense protocols in order to protect the supplies inside the company's warehouses. These defense protocols were designed to ensure that control of the headquarters would be secured through non-lethal methods.\n\t\t\t\tWhile the company's human workers followed Apollo's regulations in non-lethal control, the automated machines, however, were provided a different protocol.",
	["Cothrite Infiltrator"] = "Of course, once the Lordbreakers knew the machines weren't willing to leave any survivors, they devised a plan to shut down the headquarter's security engines.\nThat sort of plan wouldn't need more than around 10 people, however. A few teachings from the late Cothran were invaluable in breaching into a heavily protected protection sector.",
	["Extant Release"] = "Drawn from the ancient amber that sustains the Greenbelt, the ancient world rises once again.\nCaitlin sighed deeply at what she had done. In peaceful times, such amber would be used for study, not for war.\nAl-Assad would frown upon her destructive actions.",
	["Funeral Eulogist"] = "August Crissbach cradled her grandson as she wheezed on her deathbed. For the fourth time this week, the NeFoCo salesmen advertised an enzyme mist to sustain her life while the doctors could deal with her bezoar, and for the fourth time both her and David sent them away.\nHer neighbours thought her suicidal; Worse, they scorned her grandson for enabling her euthanasia by turning down the enzyme.\nSuch accusations couldn't be further from the truth; August had lived a deeply fulfilling life, full of wonderful people, wonderful sights, wonderful jobs. But that was then, and this was now. Her life was complete; No goals to pursue, no children to mother, nowhere else to explore. A life fulfilled to its fullest, with few downtimes, struggles, and regrets. Who could ask for more?\nA professional photographer in her youth, August stared gently at the weathered photograph of her decades old husband, and smiled.\nShe was the first funeral in Bloxburg in two months.",
	["Persistent Peeper"] = "With such a powerful drug coming out of nowhere and radically altering how the citizens of Bloxburg lived their lives, Eisenhower became a celebrity against his will. He did a round of talks to explain the Enzyme to people when it went public, but expressly stated it was not meant for public use.\nUnable to deal with the ceaseless waves of questions, the situation of the enzyme spiralling out of control, and the idea that maybe, just maybe, he might be responsible for all of this, Eisenhower retreated to his home and his husband.\nBut while he retreated from the world, becoming blind to the problems he's caused, all eyes were very much on Eisenhower and Artemis.",
	["Flesh Fashionista"] = "Pleasure is the purpose of life. To sit inside a room and fill your brain with dopamine and seratonin is the reason to exist. Do anything, be anything that floods your body with pleasure.\nIn contrast, pain is the antithesis of life. To experience pain is to experience deep-rooted trauma. To cause pain to yourself or to others makes you literally Hitler.\nThe PLURRAL will do anything to stop themselves from experiencing pain, and many feel extreme agony at being born human. Cats, shrimp, dogs, panthers, alligators are all such better creatures than humans, unable to think, unable to think about things that cause them pain.\nThusly do they raid the greenbelt, to become their authentic selves.",
	["Brick Heights Columnist"] = "--Excerpt from Brick Heights, Issue #58 - Is Brick Heights Biased? A response from the Editors--\nLast week, we publicly supported Astarossa's crackdown on the Smiley's and PLURRAL's illegal enzyme trade, which caused an uproar. With accusations of editorial bias being levied against us, we will now explain our position on the Enzyme and its future in the interest of transparency.\nThe Necroenzyme is the single greatest invention of this century, with its inventor possessing a level of intelligence not seen since the time of the Dwarves. However, be reminded of the Metaverse. While it allowed people to communicate across the planet, it also fomented social unrest as people were more connected to being online than with their direct peers.\nAnything strong enough to help us is also strong enough to hurt us; Doubly so with the Enzyme. \nIt is important to remember that its inventor intended only to use it on his husband, and his terrified inaction to its formula being leaked has allowed it to be used for the terrible deeds we see. Every radical change to society, from industry to the metaverse and now immortality, takes time to adjust.\nApollo Scott has taken the place of Eisenhower in the public's eye; A brave, if naïve young man who uses the Enzyme for good, and is mostly delivering on this promise. We are concerned that he is overharvesting the enzyme - a critical weakness of an Enzymic Society - and at how easy it is for the regular citizen or criminal to purchase.\nApollo has worked openly with Astarossa to corall and control the Enzyme so it is only used for good. For his austere, conservative bent, and how nakedly obvious he's using the enzyme to secure votes, Astarossa has done a tolerable job of controlling the Enzyme's negative effects. We are most concernt that his pride, beaten into him by the Demon Wars, prevents him from asking for outside assistance.\nThe Enzyme is overall a positive societal force, but a deeply dangerous one that must be controlled.",
	["Extant Titanoboa"] = "As the PLURRALs hunted the forest and her guardian, it became bloodied with ancient beings resurrected to keep her safe.\nThe last animals she resurrected ate the corpses of their fallen brethren, then struck anew into the hearts of the catgirl menace.",
	["Bloxburg's Greenbelt"] = "How would you deal with loss?\nWould you find solace in nature, trying to piece back something else so you'd feel whole as well?\nOr...\nWould you delude yourself from the painful truth of reality, ensuring you won't lose a part of yourself ever again?",
	["The PLURRALITY"] = "How would you deal with loss?\nWould you find solace in nature, trying to piece back something else so you'd feel whole as well?\nOr...\nWould you delude yourself from the painful truth of reality, ensuring you won't lose a part of yourself ever again?",
	["Ripper's Gaze"] = "Apollo screamed as he woke up, sweat flying off his body. Scrambling to hold the well-used guardrail beside his bed, the young man grit his teeth as he waited for the panic, the visions, the stench of gore to subside. Long-practiced at handling panic attacks, Apollo's breath returned to normal shortly.\nOne fateful day a decade ago, Apollo's parents were melted in front of his face as they leaped on top of him, protecting him from that callous murderer.  Wiggling his knee stubs, Apollo was grateful he didn't lose more of himself.\nBut it's been so long! I crawled on the floor for years, but look at me now! I advanced the field of Robotics by decades just to give myself four arms! I've put the man behind bars! I've perfected the Enzyme so no one else has to have their parents die like that! Why is he still haunting me after all this time I've beaten him!?\nA gust from an open window entered the room, sat on Apollo's face. It smelled of the cobblestone below, of the same petrichor he smelt as the wet shrapnel that was once his father was smeared across his face.\nApollo rocked back and forth, a gibbering wreck.",
	["Remove All Traces"] = "As a child, Thec Hiller lived in the Vakroyd Woods, a dangerous location where everything is trying to kill you.\nHunting with his parents for food from a young age, he learnt which berries were safe and which ones aren't, which parts of an animal don't need to be cooked and which ones will kill you even if you do.\nHe gained his fascination for chemicals in his childhood too, when he observed a deer merrily munching on a slushberry bush and not literally evacuating out all of its organs. That happens when a human eats them; It's what claimed his uncle. The sight deeply offended him; How did this lowly creature we all eat survive something us supreme beings couldn't?\nA bright lad whose impoverished parents wanted his potential realised, they forked over everything to get his education at Robloxcity, one of the many cities offering cheap accommodation and tuition to help rebuild after the Demon Wars. Gaining renown as a masterful yet snobbish chemist, Thec experimented on all sorts of materials, animals, people, studying which ones withstand which toxins and acids in which doses. He would experiment on himself if the test subjects were low, his skin and face turning stark white from the abuse over the years.\nHe felt his life's work was done when he killed a deer with a slash from a blade coated from a formula developed from that same slushberry bush. He sneered at the liquifying deer, its subversion of the natural order now put in place. But the overlay gave Thec a level of grim fascination not felt since that deer in his childhood; Cothrite, Javionese, Katharan, Forothian peoples and all the animals they've brought! Will they survive his formula?\nEyeing two Havaluvian entrepreneurs and their child, Thec coated his trusty scythe once again. The hunt was on.",
	["Big Rush Crush"] = "With Astarossa distracted by the Astral Faith that had so poisoned his party, The smileys snuck into the Town Hall...",
	["Emporium Farmer"] = "Ever wondered where those Pet Eggs in those simulator games come from? Look no further than the Egg Emporium! Situated in the Hell of Prosperity, Egg Emporium seeks to provide simulator developers a good supply of Pet Eggs to fill up their machines with. These lovable animals have been trained to support their masters in a wide variety of money collecting effortss.\nWhat's the secret to making so many eggs? Well, good fertilizer and work ethic, of course!",
	["Pet Egg"] = "With friends like these by your side, you won't have to worry about simulating alone!\n\t\tYou don't even need to feed or take care of them.",
	Pet = "With friends like these by your side, you won't have to worry about simulating alone!\n\t\tYou don't even need to feed or take care of them.",
	["Emporium Firemage"] = "Our team of Vitality Demons are well trained in taking care of the Pet Eggs you love to crack open in bulk. From Basic to Superextrasupreflendouserror Neon, you can trust that our supplies will be top-notch quality!",
	["Emporium Herder"] = "If you ever wonder where those pets you discard go to, don't worry! Those fellers will be back in our pens in no time. Soon enough, they'll find a new owner that'll be their new best friend. No need to feel guilty!",
	["Egg Empire Emporium"] = "So, what're you waiting for, developers and players? Come on down to Egg Emporium and get yourself a Pet Egg or Pet Egg Machine today!",
	["Rift of the Vundebted"] = "\"...Oh? You want to know the actual secret to the Pet Eggs?\n\t\tLet's just say our business' relationship with those shoddy simulators is a lot more than just monetary purchases...\"",
	["Emporium Soulbinder"] = "\"It's a simple method, really. Most simulator developers, if not all of them, have a tinge of greed in their soul. With products like ours and the possible profits they can attain, they wouldn't even think of checking what's inside of them.\nPoor Umberhallow had to rule over a single gladiator pit to attain the Revelry he needed. I, however, can simply mooch off the wasted lives of the avid brainnumb consumers of petty coin collector games.\"",
	["Emporium Salesdevil"] = "\"I've seen it, the amount of money people burn on cookie cutter coin collectors. Double coins, double storage, double luck, you name it. They really go heads over heels for rising numbers, it's fascinating. If not money, they'll spend time. Time is such a valuable resource nowadays, y'know? If they're going to waste it, we might as well pick up the remains for ourselves.\"",
	["Emporium Ad Designer"] = "\"There's also something peculiar regarding the artistic nature of those simulators. It doesn't matter how polished or aesthetically pleasing they are, as long as they fulfill the need to give people instant gratification. Really, the people who they placate to must be either idiotic or masochistic. While profits do interest me, I have a high respect for artistic integrity. If the creators of those time wasters won't spend the effort in making their worlds interesting, I'll make sure their Pets are.\"",
	["Controlled Scarcity"] = "\"...Besides, aesthetical pleasure is an important aspect. You have to make sure some pets look fantastic, captivating even. Neon stripes, bright colors, a mess of slathered effects are all you need to make any pet look important. Soon enough, you'll have people spending dollars in two digits every time they pick off a stick from the haystack in hopes of finding that legendary needle... then be captivated once more by the next expensive, much larger haystack.\"",
	["Asmodeus, Emporium Proprieter"] = "\"People have criticized me before regarding my business. They call me immoral, supporting a predatory trend of entrancing players into a monotonous parasitic game covered in glitter and crayons. I disagree, of course. My view on it is different.\n\nIn this world, profit blinds the weak. People blame the creators of those games since they would be uncomfortable with the truth of their appeal. To tell you the truth, both my customers and their customers are part of the problem. People of greed... and people who seek instant gratification. Predatory business is deplorable, but their effectiveness hinges on the desperation of the feeble. They would rather forfeit their minds to a world that cares not of morals or self, for their deepest desires is achieving any sense of progress without pain to their physical bodies.\n\nSoon enough, they become as parasitic as the creators who placate them. Who knows what their obsession entails for their real lives? Of course, the proof lay infront of your eyes; the Discarded.\nDo you think they see their Pets as actual friends, things with real emotions? No. They see them as nothing more than machines meant to assist them in their conquest for wealth, whether material or emotional. Once they've been outclassed, they're gone without a second thought. ...Hah, pitiful, don't you think?\n\nAt the very least, those Pets have one owner they can continue benefitting, whether they like it or not.\n\nMe.\"",
	["Rock-Star Impstrument"] = "\"You've heard of Hell's Band, yes? The sinner rehabalitation group arranged with Shedletsky in order to grant the dwellers of Hell a chance to go up to Heaven?\nI was an avid listener... and boy, was I once a bratty one.\"",
	["Soul-Star Chorus Familiar"] = "\"That group had most genres under their collection. Rock, Jazz, Rock Jazz, Classical, Classical Rock, Classical Jazz, Classical Rock Jazz... you name it.\nThey even had Ludwig van Blockhaven as one of their players once. He managed to ascend within less than a day!\"",
	["Pop-Star Substitune"] = "\"They were even recruiting young imps into their ranks. Some of them were truly exceptional in their field.\n...the rest were a bit insufferable.\"",
	["Devil's Chord"] = "\"...I might be getting ahead of myself... Yes, seriously! Rock, Jazz, Classical! They covered all three of those! A bit of Pop and Reggae too! They were insane!\"",
	["Spirit Melody"] = "\"...I might be getting ahead of myself... Yes, seriously! Rock, Jazz, Classical! They covered all three of those! A bit of Pop and Reggae too! They were insane!\"",
	["Light-Motif"] = "\"...I might be getting ahead of myself... Yes, seriously! Rock, Jazz, Classical! They covered all three of those! A bit of Pop and Reggae too! They were insane!\"",
	["Serotonin Battery"] = "When Enzyme-infused tissue connects to another host, its regenerative process becomes unstable. The body struggles to decide which life to sustain — the donor’s or the host’s. The result is uncontrolled mutation, both physical and mental.\n\nDuring the chaos of Caitlin’s assault, Sarah Greene Bailey desperately sought survival through experimental grafts of Enzyme-infused material. The strain shattered her mind, leaving behind only fragments of who she once was. Now, she and her remaining followers wander as hollow echoes of their former selves — drawn to the energy of the Enzyme, unable to live without it.\n\nTheir purpose twisted, their empathy drained, they roam the outskirts of Bloxburg spreading the Enzyme’s curse, believing they are relieving others of pain. The beginning of the new outbreak... starts here.\n",
	["Growling Guardian"] = "Astarossa's dying words weigh heavily on Kingrin's mind; More powerful forces than the Smileys may arrive and hurt them for the enzyme. This tool to bring back his comrades doesn't keep them safe; It endangers them.\n\nSeeing the PLURRAL horde assault Bloxburg, the citizens flock to the reviled Smileys for protection. Kingrin's response, to protect these outsiders over his own kin, stunned the Familey. Many considered it a betrayal.\nBut Kingrin knows better; There is no Familey without Bloxburg, and no Bloxburg if it's overran by mutant catgirls.\n\nCan a monster atone for its sins?",
	["Apate, Demon Investor"] = "Apollo's gruelling brawl with Thec was ended by the woman he's learnt to fear the most.\nMcKayla Newman has destroyed the enzyme supply that keeps his company afloat, and without his intervention two hundred thousand zombified lives will be lost.\n\nWith the NeFoCo CEO leaving during this time of crisis, the board of directors has entered a state of emergency.\nThe angel investor that poured the most capital to found the NeFoCo has taken his mantle, and he vows to turn a profit on what little of the Necroforensics Corporation remains.\n\nPectus Excavatum.",
	["Checkpoint Security"] = "Half the plan is complete. With the Enzyme supply cut off, the Lordbreakers can pressure Astarossa to stop creating more zombified citizens as he panics to keep those on it safe.\n...But when they learn of his disappearance, of how there will not be an Astarossa to protect half the zombified population, many Lordbreakers panic. Did they just consign two hundred thousand people to death by starvation?\nMcKayla disagrees. It's harsh, but they signed their lives away when they took the enzyme.\n\nTheir contingency to the PLURRAL horde is to close the city off, prevent any zombified people from leaving. If they cannot cure the disease of immortality, they will quarantine it, prevent its spread.\n\nIt is better to live quadriplegic and blind than it is to live forever.",
	["Ancient Egg"] = "With Caitlin falling to Sarah and Catlyn, the Arkhive have scattered. Unable to protect the Greenbelt from the rampaging PLURRAL horde.\nBeing the syndicate least reliant on the enzyme, the Arkhive have lost the most of any faction, but will also come out of the apocalypse the best off.\n\nStill, many Arkhivists doubt Caitlin's choice to revive Grimclaw. The dragons almost conquered Robloxia aeons ago, during the time of Shedletsky.\nSo they keep tabs on him, to know if they've traded one terrible outcome for another.\n\nThe time for mourning the fallen will come after the nightmare is over; Caitlin wouldn't have it any other away.",
	["Monument to Hubris"] = "The CRP had been struggling with an internal feud - Between the sensible, rational, optional immortality of Astarossa and the fanatical, forced immortality of the Astral Faith.\nWith the leader of the rational faction removed, the CRP has become a dogmatic cult, hellbent on ending the sinful stain of mortality in their holy city.\n\nBeing mortal is a burden to society, much like smoking or obesity. Governments rightly add taxes to smoking and sugar to punish those who harm society; Senescence is no different.\nUnder LeBlanc's lead, the CRP will make choosing to be mortal, choosing to be a burden illegal.\n\n[\"Feral Citizen\"] = [[Well, that screwed me over! Enzyme's running out the clock on this dapper gentleman. Funny how the drug to make me live forever cut me life short, huh?\n\nBut a good citizen still helps those in need, right?",
	["Patchwork of Disease"] = "With the enzyme becoming a scarce commodity, zombified people found creative solutions to their starvation. \n\nSome hunted the near-extinct gharials for the enzyme.\nSome stole it from others.\nSome cooked up their own highly dangerous enzymic broth.\n\nLarger beings need proportionally less enzyme for each pound of biomass. Because of this, the most peaceful of the bunch stuck together, sharing what little of the enzyme they have with each other, sharing their suffering.",
	["Flesh Centrifuge"] = "The Patchworks were masters of their own reconstruction. Every adjustment had to be perfect — a single misalignment, a single flawed connection, and their delicate balance would collapse into chaos.\n",
	["Overwhelmed Ambulance"] = "Many a doctor swore curses upon McKayla's name on the night the NeFoCo's enzyme stockpile was destroyed. Their operations went from sustainable in the morning to a class-5 emergency in the night, and without Astarossa to divert emergency resources into enzyme production or create curfews to control the citizenry, the hospitals found themselves overwhelmed by a swarm of A&E patients begging for the enzyme or with other health conditions.\n\nThus are the necrosyndicates held accountable for Bloxburg's decay.",
	["Botanical Beggar"] = "Arnold stopped trying to grab the trimmer.\nWhile it did make you immortal, the Necroenzyme caused most bodily functions to cease, including the immune system. Arnold overslept and forgot his hospital appointment last week as a thorny rose pricked his thigh.\nAnd with the hospital overwhelmed with enzyme beggars, seems like he won't be rebooking that appointment any time soon.\n\nAt least he'll make a nice rosebush.",
	["Corporate Discipline"] = "As he took over the NeFoCo, Apate entered the corporation into administration, selling off as much as he can and proposing business plans to ensure this company will survive without its founding inventor.\nHe decided there were two problems to remedy:\n\nA) Workplace culture was lazy and overstaffed, which put people's lives and wellbeing over profits.\nThe stockpile responsible for keeping Bloxburg alive was all in one place? Barely guarded to the point a swarm of citizens and an edgy chemist could overwhelm them? Why did these workers not kill the lordbreakers as they assaulted company property?\n\nB) The business was too focused on public utility in one single city, and should diversify its portfolio and products.\nConferring with another company he invested in, one that sells weapons and materiel to the warlords of the Vakroyd Desert, they seemed very interested in the innovative Zoomba technology.\n\nWith a genius flash of insight, Apate realised these two problems had the same solution. His warlord associates will love their new armaments.",
	["Emergency Rations"] = "With hundreds of Lordbreakers spread thin around Bloxburg, it was increasingly difficult to spread resources to the populace. Although, that didn't stop the provisions to its fighters; muesli and crackers were given to all that needed it, and those that needed it would get it, no matter what.",
	["Shady Supplier"] = "With the enzyme's supply massively reduced, many people started manufacturing it in their home, either by taking pre-made enzyme and diluting it, or using lesser-quality substitutes such as extracts from those taking the enzyme.\n\nA small cottage industry formed, both out of necessity to stay alive, and to make a quick buck.",
	["Synthetic Enzyme"] = "The thing about homebrewed substances is you don't know what's in them or what they'll do to you. Would you trust the man on the street to give you that important medicine?",
	["Twisted Turret"] = "And you're naturally asking: What if it's defective?\n\nY'see, sometimes they use the regenerating bodies of fallen zombies in these homebrewed enzymes. And if they're not careful, some of their skin tissue or what have you gets in there. A good 25% of these shady enzyme vials have this defect, turning the drinker into a monster.\n\nAnd you don't want that to happen...",
	["Enzyme Runner"] = "The enzyme cookers needed to get their enzyme from somewhere in order to dilute it. The most ruthless had few qualms about taking it from others.",
	["Arkomms Technician"] = "\"Nina?\"\n'Jake. Have you found her?'\n\"Yes. Respirator broken, brain removed. No other harm to the body. Time of death seems to be six hours ago. Grimclaw nowhere to be seen.\"\n'Copy that. Extract her blackbox and return to the outskirts of Robloxcity.'\n\"...I think we should carry her to base and bury her.\"\n'Negative. Too dangerous. We'll come back for her wh-'\n\"I understand you want to be professional right now, but she was a big sister to you. To all of us. There's no telling what those freaks will do to her corpse. Please, Nina. Let me bring her back.\"\n'...'\n'...'\n'...'\n\"Nina? Respond.\"\n'...R-roger that, Jake. Return her to base.'",
	["Astral Faith Biohacker"] = "\"It appears the heretics are on the move.\"\n\"It's time, then. Do not let them succeed.\"",
	["Astral Ruination"] = "\"We cannot let them take away the gift bestowed onto us.\"",
	["While Stocks Last"] = "While the hell of the PLURRAL invasion of Bloxburg unfolded, people were desperate to stay alive with the Enzyme. Many hoped that they could hold on until the CRP or Arkhive or Eisenhower or Anyone stabilised the enzyme supply.\n\nApate's enzyme stockpile, the last of the NeFoCo's, was exactly what these desperate folk needed, and he's a generous man!\nLet's sell as much of it as he can to the highest bidder. If you really need it, you'll sell all your worldly possessions for it, right?\n\nThe helicopter behind the bidding stood at the ready in case the horde invaded this little auction. Braindead catgirls are not good customers.",
	["A Legendary Gathering"] = "Two scientists met together. The one who created the necroenzyme, and the one who popularised it.\n\nBoth had made many mistakes in its usage; Eisenhower cared only for his fiancé that he leaked it, and was too scared to take responsibility for his creation, leading to important information about its functions lost.\nApollo was too preoccupied thinking of all the good the enzyme could do that he failed to take any precautions for its abuse, leading to zoombas.\n\nThe others in Eisenhower's lab felt similar; The remnants of the CRP, unable to protect their leader or the city.\nKingrin, who destroyed the city's leader to protect his enzyme trade only to realise that trade put his family in danger.\nAnd McKayla, who's hellbent drive for prevent a second Biggs has come at such a steep cost.\n\nThe necrosyndicates have been held accountable for Bloxburg's decay, and they intend to rectify their mistakes. It was only in working together that this nightmare could possibly end.",
	["Apocalypse Rising"] = "It would either end or continue forever, decaying all the while.",
	["Eric Newman"] = "The dusty armoury doors swing open. With the flick of a lightswitch, decades old lightbulds illuminated the room. Ten farmers enter, equipping themselves with firearms and vests.\n\n\"Got everything?\"\n\"Yup.\"\n\"Let's go take our town back.\"",
	["Scour the City"] = "The contingency plan was simple enough:\n\nEisenhower would manufacture as much of the Counterenzyme as he could, made from Grimclaw's moonbreath. He'd give some to Apollo and use it to help clean up the stragglers. Artemis, and only Artemis, would be allowed to stay alive with the Enzyme in future.\n\nApollo would descend into the depths of Bloxburg's wellspring, and use a sample of the counterenzyme to hack the failsafe left there during the Demon Wars. This will neutralise every zombie within Bloxburg.\n\nThis meant that no zombie could escape. The lordbreakers would set up checkpoints to get any mortal person out of Bloxburg, and to stop the zombified from escaping. They wouldn't know they were about to die.\n\nBut that still left the question of the elusive monster that was once Sarah. She's in bloxburg somewhere, but with no confirmed sightings for the past three hours, someone would have to find and neutralise this hulking mass of flesh and pleasure.\n\nThis is where the Smileys came in.",
	["Harrison Powell"] = "The smileys expected the citizenry to hate them as they always did, but they helped the gang with open arms. They may be horrible murderers, but they're Bloxburg's horrible murderers. Being... Liked by that. By strangers. It was a peculiar feeling, one that Kingrin couldn't quite place. He was just as violent as before, but that carnal art he specialised in was being put towards a selfless use for once.\n\nEven in death, Astarossa rules this city; Kingrin had become a willing pawn in his Contingency. The thought of being beneath him should make Kingrin recoil in disgust, but he felt... Happy to be a part of the puzzle. Happy to protect others.\n\nThe mask slipped so that the man may once again live.",
	["Captain Skewerglee"] = "His tolerance of outsiders - His open support of them - Was controversial within the Smiley Familey.",
	["Grey, Mending the Lost"] = "Messiah Hospital has a lot of grief over the PLURRAL horde. They intimiately knew the doctor that started it all.\n\nStudying incapacitated catgirls, some of the doctors learnt the lobotomisation technique that causes them to feel only pleasure doesn't remove parts of the brain; It weakens the parts that experience pain and suffering.\nThis meant that, it could be undone. This is how Messiah Hospital will atone for failing to stop its top doctor from breaking down.",
	["Apex of Fantasy"] = "As Sarah laid there in the open grass, she laughed at her predicament.\nThere was no possible way she'd be taken back by her hospital. Defilation of graveyards and pilfering of morgues are the worst crimes she could have commited.\nLaughter turned to pained gasps, pained gasps turn into choking cries.\nFor the first time, she's used the necroenzyme on herself. What she once sought for comfort had now taken over her life.\n\nShe crouched down and sobbed, the pain in her arm growing stronger.",
	["Jestorder's Failsafe"] = "The Demon Wars were a complex, intergenerational conflict lasting from 150 AD to 388 AD, starting from the rediscovery and assassination of the Alpha Brick's protector by a mercenary group known as \"The Stagnation,\" it saw the apex of demonkind's control over robloxia, with every settlement pledging feudal fealty to a demon to \"protect\" it from other demons.\n\nNestled between two lakes and a mountain, Bloxburg traded hands several times over the course of its founding halfway into the Demon Wars by Herrus, later Zeige Siksis and the ultimate victor of the Demon Wars, a revel demon known as Jestorder.\n\nAstarossa fought in the last 20 years of the Demon Wars, initially a common soldier conscripted to fight Jestorder before becoming a colonel earnestly hating the prankster; Jestorder would hide studbombs underneath each of his ill-gotten settlements that would destroy all demons of a different stud bias to him, causing untold casualties and cruelty to those retaking his property.\n\nIt was Jestorder's betrayal by a lowly Lieutenant Umberhallow that ultimately ended the Demon War and wider demonic hegemony over robloxia, but the scars of the century-spanning war can still be felt after the Overlay if you know where to look; Astarossa has a keen eye for its artifice. \n\nGiven how the bomb was harmless to non-demons, Astarossa kept Jestorder's contraption underneath Bloxburg untouched. It would be useful if the Four Hells return en masse, or if some demonic civilians turn to terrorism to restore their unearnt prestige during the Demon Wars.\n\nHe never wanted to use the studbomb to destroy zombified people, nor did he expect that it would; A talented leader prepares for the worst case scenario.\n\nThe bomb will implode, but on whose side will it fall? McKayla and Apollo destroying the zombified, or the Astral Faith destroying the living?\nBoth parties believe them to be following Astarossa's orders. \nEven in death, Astarossa rules Bloxburg.",
	["The Killer"] = "So this is what dying feels like.\nI feel the warmth of my own blood, as I lay, unable to move.\nI feel it all, in truth. The blow crushed my left temporal bone, the shards lodged in my brain.\nAh... the way my face froze up. Longitudinal fractures tend to do that. Just how hard did she hit me? Too much force, and facial paralysis kicks in. Always took away the fun...\n\nFire and smoke crash through the doorways. I try to cover my mouth, to no avail.\nEven if I could move, the brat had turned my arm to ash.\n\nTaking his legs wasn't enough... I'll gouge his eyes next, and pour the mix in his empty sockets! Turn his hands to stumps! Force his new friend to watch too! AhhHAhahhhahaHAHAHA!!!\n\n...\n\nI wasn't getting out.\n\nTo die like this, to be left behind. My life's work... cut short. I couldn't stomach the idea of not seeing it through: Bloxburg had been mine to use. Thousands, left intact. Tears swole up at the thought of it all going to waste. I was going to expose what separated US from THEM. THAT'S why they feared my name. \n\nThe black smoke filled the room and my lungs.\n\nFor it all to end, with me-\n\n\"Being forgotten?\"\n\nThe smoke had formed the shape of a man, black as obsidian. His face, unmoving and frowning.\nYet he spoke:\n\n\"You moved people's hearts and minds into darkness. A wound that is not easily forgotten.\"\n\nHe moved closer to me. His eyes, beaming with light.\n\n\"And for as long as that memory remains, so will you. Living on, forever claiming more hearts.\nYou will continue your hunt with us, now. For our age draws near.\"\n\nI could see his face better now.\n\n\"Wipe those tears, and take my hand.\"\n\"Let them see your smile.\"\n\nIt was a mask.",
	["Decaying Protector"] = "It was clear to all the zombified citizens: The NeFoCo's stockpile collapsing meant that their time was suddenly limited. Many won't survive the sudden price hike that would happen until the enzyme stockpile could regrow.\n\nThe reactions was mixed; Some resorted to gross rituals and procedures barely distinguishable from necromancy. Others became pathetic rodents, going beyond theft and murder, to obtain mere drops of the life-sustaining enzyme.\n\nBut a noble few made sure their last moments were worth remembering.\n",
	["Enzymic Saviours"] = "Those who were due their enzyme shots were going to starve to death first. One by one they fell, scattered by the PLURRAL horde.\n\nBut they were never going to give up. Though they may not see it, they have a city to save, a dawn to ensure happens.",
	["Euphoric Vengeance"] = "The PLURRAL horde held a special place in their furry hearts for those who sold the enzyme en masse. They perplexed the catgirls: They sell the brain-no-hurt-juice, but still have hurty-brains that feel pain? \n\nSarah remembered many of these dealers; Those that had extorted others into taking the enzyme, who badgered mourning families to return their loved ones.\nHow great it felt to eat their marrow, eat their enzyme! Their removal from the world has made it a much happier place.",
	Unburden = "Intelligence is considered a curse amongst the PLURRAL horde - If you can think, that means you can think bad thoughts. That means you can think about pain. Thinking is evil. Surrender your thoughts, your feelings, individuality. You exist to make happy little chemicals in your brain.\n\nThe process of \"unburdening\" yourself - Lobotomising your brain to be less able to feel pain, only happiness - Used to be a labour-intensive effort on Sarah's end. Not now, though, for her surgical abilities combined with the enzyme's mutagenic properties have combined to create an efficient infectious disease. \n\nIgnorance is bliss.",
	["Violent Larcenist"] = "While originally advocating for the Javionese diaspora, the lordbreakers during the time of the necrosyndicates expanded to include anyone opposed to the enzyme.\nA question remained for them; What should be done about those that've already took it?\n\nSome proposed allowing them to live to the age of seventy before taking their enzyme supplies off them.\nSome proposed letting them have two years of life before the enzyme was destroyed.\nSome proposed letting them all live in a zoo while they starve to death.\nOthers were more extreme still...",
	["The Chairman"] = "\"...Awh, jeez... Big Brutus and the Terrorizing Tomboy aren't around the districts?\"\n\"THOSE SUBSTANTIAL SUBJECTS AREN'T IN THE CITY! NOWHERE!\"\n\"Aw heaven... guess we'll have to make due with Boy Genius and his exploits... Take a lot of photos of the fight over there, by the way! Bonus points since there's religion involved, Kara and the crowd are gonna love it!\"\n\"SUBSTANTIALITY'S COMIN'!!!\"\n\"Right on, lil' imp boy!\"",
	["McKayla Newman"] = "McKayla walked out of the estate, pressing against her amputation wound.\nThe night felt cold. Each step back towards civilization was agonizing.\n...the worries of what might happen when she has to bring the bad news to the Familey made it worse.\n\nThe grass and leaves of the forest floor crunched beneath her feet. The sound of a blazing fire roared behind her.\n...She just wanted to go home... back to a place she remembered... a place she saw as home; freed from this idiotic\nsituation of rebirth and exploitation. She wanted Bloxburg to return to normalcy again.\n...the sights of people begging for their loved ones to be kept alive hit her like a sharp knife against her heart.\nBut she couldn't bear to help them, either. It was ignoring them... or leave Bloxburg in the maws of people like Biggs Cradshaw.\n\nShe looked at the night-lit city, a deep breath of anticipation entering her lungs.\n...and prayed for the safety of the once-misguided inventor she wronged.",
	["Hack the Failsafe"] = "\"Status?\"\n\"Terminal One is unlocked. Apollo Scott is currently breaching into Terminal Two with back-up from NeFoCo employees. Intel suggests Astral Faith movement on Terminal Three.\"\n\"...Chance of success?\"\n\"...roughly 50%.\"\n\"Understood.\"",
	["Mortal Dawn"] = "\"The architects of the Necrosyndicate Crisis were deeply regretful that 200,000 zombified people died at their actions. Yet the Protobabylonian horde, yet the Astral Faith's schemes, yet that monstrous remnant of Sarah Greene Bailey forced their hand.\"\n\t\t- Herrus' Archives, MCMXCVIIIa",
	["Immortal Dusk"] = "\"While the forces against zealous immortality fought valiantly, the half of Bloxburg's 400,000 population to not take the enzyme perished with the Failsafe's detonation. The small yet dangerous chapters of the Astral Faith abused their immortality to subjugate other Robloxian settlements, returning Robloxia to the feudal ages the Demon Wars were fought to escape from.\"\n\t\t",
	["Lay Siege to Sadness"] = "\"So that's it,\" Eisenhower mused, cowering underneath a table.\n\"We're done for. Bloxburg's done for. And it's all my fault. It's all... There's nothing more that I can do.\"\nKingrin turned around from the door he was guarding, growled, and grabbed Eisenhower by the throat, slamming him against the stony wall.\n\n\"YOU PILLOCK! YOUR BOYFRIEND DIED. DIED! SO YOU COULD KILL THAT THING!\nIS THIS HOW YOU'RE GOING TO REPAY HIM? BY SITTING AROUND, DOING NOTHING?\"\nEisenhower choked against the burly man's iron grip.\n\n\"YOU, A REVOLTING WASTE OF A YOUNG MAN, CREATED SOMETHING THAT HAS CHANGED MY CITY, THIS PLANET, FOREVER. AND YOU'RE TELLING ME YOU CAN'T KILL A GIANT ZOMBIE CATGIRL?\"\n\n\"But it's my fault! I-I, if I never made the enzyme\"\n-Then we'd not be in this mess! I get it, mate!\" A weirdly chipper Kingrin dropped the young inventor, allowing him to regain his composure.\n\n\"But you did. We all make terrible mistakes. Mine was slaughtering thousands to be respected. Yours was playing god.\nSo what are you going to do?\"\n\nThe moaning miasma indicated the monster that was once Sarah was honing in on their location. Kingrin picked up his hammer, turned to face the door.\n\n\"You know what's in this lab. You have to have something.\nFor once in your fucking life. Take accountability and do something about your incompetence. Maybe then you'll deserve your 'boyfriend.'\"\n\nKingrin charged out of the door.",
	["Eisenhower, World Ablaze"] = "With the last vial of the counterenzyme, Eisenhower regained his composure. That brute was right; All of this was ultimately Eisenhower's fault, but that doesn't excuse inaction. That doesn't excuse cowardice. That doesn't excuse wasting his boyfriend's sacrifice.\n\nNo ordinary man could beat that monster in fair combat.\nKingrin was many things, but he was still just a man.\n\nThe monster that was once Sarah lurched into the doorframe of the last room in the laboratory. Kingrin's head slithered out of her arm, and the burly man spoke once more.\n\n\"You've nowhere else to run. Nowhere else to hide. I-I can fix you... I can make you happy...\"\n\nEisenhower, a gibbering wreck, took a deep sigh.\n\"Good. It wouldn't be a fair fight if I could escape.\"",
	["Face your Failures"] = "\"I can fix you! I can make you happy! I can give you back your boyfriend!\"\n\nEisenhower's brain was overwhelmed with pure rage. He knew that if he stopped and thought about Sarah's offer for even a second, he would doubt himself. Doubt his actions. He would accept it. He would become happy.\n\nBut that's not what he has to do. He has to own up and be accountable for sending Bloxburg to hell!\n\nAnd that is exactly what he will do.",
	["The Failsafe Altered"] = "The counterenzyme-infused napalm burnt away Sarah's body and mind, and even still Eisenhower felt worse.\n\n\tThis would be a traumatising night. Eisenhower fell down to the ashen stone flooring and sobbed, grieving for everything he - and Bloxburg - had lost.\n\n\t\tThe lordbreakers were overran by the catgirl horde, by the astral faith mobsters trying to take control over Bloxburg. The checkpoints were nearly overrun.\n\n\t\tEric Newman swatted away a catgirl, finding himself surrounded by eighteen of the blighters.\n\n\t\t\"This is it. You did your best, McKayla. We all did. That's all that matters...\" Eric closed his eyelids and accepted his death.\n\n\t\t...\n\n\t\t...\n\n\t\t...\n\n\t\t...\n\n\t\t...\n\n\t\t...\n\n\t\tEric opened his eyelids, deeply confused.",
	["Nina Hellensoft"] = "Caitlin's Corpse was a tight fit for her cedar coffin, the first of Bloxburg's coffins in a long time and hopefully the first of many.\n\nWith Grimclaw's sudden and unexplained disappearance, it was presumed he was up to no good. The Arkhive had a new purpose: To figure out what happened to that living artifact of ancient history or his progeny. To make sure they behave.\n\nBut that's in the future. For now, Al-Assad gave deep platitudes to his favourite student at her funeral. Caitlin will be remembered as a hero, not of the same importance as Dukran or Shedletsky but certainly of the same calibre.\n\nThe new Head Archaeologist of the Arkhive placed a magnetic sword on Caitlin's coffin, an old burial rite in Alar culture. She mused that one day, she will be in a similar coffin, with adoring students sad to see her go, doing the same rite.\nThus the cycle of life and death, of archaeology continues.",
	["Devin Conway"] = "It was not only the Arkhivists that were at Caitlin's funeral. Many lordbreakers attended as a death. Many of the Smiley attended to pay respects to someone cool enough to die valiantly trying to stop Sarah before she became a monster.\n\nThe most unexpected person also attended; Someone who fled from Caitlin when she was at her weakest. Someone who still wished to be with her.",
	["Permission to Move On"] = "In some ways, Caitlin's funeral was a celebration. Of the person, of Bloxburg, of mortality.\n\nNow that the nightmare is over, Bloxburg can heal.",
	["Brutal Justice MK.III"] = "Excerpt from document 103-A, Recovered from the Investor's office of the NecroForensics Corporation\n\nConflict, is an eternal force in our world, one which drives us to fight for what we believe is right, one which comes at great sacrifice, and has us follow in the path of those who are determined the victors, The one's whose cause has been justified by their victory.\n\nMost of us are familiar with conflict and how its driven our history, The Demon wars, The war across the Vecross region, The old wars of strife, each of these has made a drastic impact on our world as a result of the ones who prevailed, and their justice brought upon it.\n\nSo what I propose to you, leaders of New Robloxia...\n\nWhat if you could buy your own Justice?",
	["Alexander-Pfeffel van Buren"] = "The news of his brother's death had only reached him the day after. Rapid steps echoed throughout the Buren household as Astarossa rushed out to Povvo Street. Seeing Alexander's state, his expression could only be descripted as paralyzed.\n\nThe funeral was closed-casket, sparing his loved ones from having to see his disfigured corpse. Out of everyone who showed up, the only one who knew what he looked like underneath was the man who stood by his side.\n\nWhen the guests had left, the man weeped as he embraced his wife. A breakdown that nary even the Demon Wars compared to.\nThe man cried and cried and cried. He cried till there were no tears left to shed. \nTill there was nothing left but a burning desire to lead his town to prosperity.\n\nThe same town his brother loved.",
	["Fluffle, One Deer Army"] = "Against his will has he walked the demonic land for four hundred years.\nUnable to die and unable to follow the arcane courtly rules of Demonic society, he was forced into the underworld of the underworld, selling his blade to the highest bidder.\n\nThis line of work requires a heavy heart, one our hero has come to possess. Unable to die, he has found his life stagnant beyond all measure.\n\nHe forgoes all worldly possessions except his blade and his money. Stashed away in his homeless hovel is the wealth of billionaires, all to be used to one purpose: An end to his boring existence.\n\nA mere whisper of his name is enough to silence dissent and force a business deal through.\nHis name?",
	["Scout of Stagnation"] = "Every time Fluffle thought he had gotten used to waking up somewhere completely different, he was always proven wrong. He never knew where he would wake up, he never knew how he was told who to kill. This teleportation did have benefits, though. That curry the Elder dominion demon insisted he be treated to was so spicy as to send him to bed with a stomach screaming in pain, yet he woke up with no pain, no soreness, no hangover.\n\nThe neon district was nothing like the smog-clogged fortress he slept in, but he had no time to bask in its splendor. His target, unusually close to him, was Count Celes, a Pumpkindread. Elder Revel demon, proprietor of the Funderworld's Pits.\n\nIt was time to visit the wealthiest of all demonkind.",
	["Agent of Count Celes"] = "Fluffle threw the woman down four flights of fancy spiral staircase, landing face-first on gilded tiling. She pleaded with the immortal assassin to spare her life. \nOnly one thing would; A prize greater than money. Death.\n\n...But quadrupling the bounty on her if Fluffle worked for her instead was the next best thing. Four times the wealth meant a cure could be found four times faster, yes? It would anger Kgxraqyt, and he might hunt for something that could kill him. Better yet, Fluffle could kill her when he did her job, to obtain even more chances at ending his life. \n\nAnd so Celes sent the immortal assassin on his merry way, to kill a bastard human far above his stature.\nShe was saving that money to buy each of her eighteen daughters a new superyacht, but she thinks they'd appreciate their mum over another mobile home.",
	["Agent of Alex"] = "The Elder Vitality demon knew that the immortal assassin, the first genuine threat to his secret, would be coming. And there was little he could do about it.\n\nBefore the fight even began, he pleaded with Fluffle to explain what he wanted. It wasn't wealth; Alex knew Fluffle had that in spades. What was he waiting to spend that wealth on?\n\nThe deer replied in a ton mocking the demon's inferior origins: \"123 for death.\"\n\nAnd so, the Elder vitality Demon promised him death, if he could do a job for him. Everyone knew Alex had a secret he spent whole life protecting, but none had gotten close to learning the truth. None except the Elder Thought Demon, who controls the Stunderworld. For Alex's sake, for the universe's sake, that curiosity had to be culled. Do that, and Fluffle would be granted promised death.\n\nAnd so he became an agent for three of four elders. Play them off one another, and maybe one will finally grant him his wish.",
	["Synchronised Sleep"] = "The underworld is composed of Four Hells, one for each colour of stud.\n\nThe Gunderworld is the abode of the Dominion demons, who take free will as currency. Those who work are paid in freedom, those in debt lose all choice.\nIn contrast, the Funderworld is where the Revel demons play, an endless utopia of excitement and fun, with your emotions being the payment for entry.\nThe vital energies of the Sunderworld ensured long health for its inhabitants, and illness for those that break its arcane social rules.\n\nAnd the Stunderworld? That is Herrus' domain, where the strongest have endless memory and knowledge, and the punishment for stepping out of line is to have your brain and eyes removed.\n\nThusly, he knew what Fluffle's condition was, and he was deeply interested in telling.",
	["Traverse the Four Hells"] = "When someone enters the underworld, their biases in personalities, actions, inclinations doom them to which underworld they enter.\n\nBut Fluffle was so perfectly aligned, so aggravatingly centrist, that he could not be claimed so easily. So he broke. Where once there was one, now there are four. \nHe is unable to die until they are all together.\nUnable to live until they are all whole once again.\n\n\nIf he could combine them all, Fluffle could finally get the wish he promised for.",
	["Seminal Catastrophe"] = "The Four Hells, 266 AD.\nAn immortal mercenary finds himself embroiled at the centre of a conspiracy as four elder demons pay him to eliminate the competition.\n\nLearn of the seminal catastrophe that spawned the 200-year long Demon Wars.\n\nThe battle that ensued was tremendous; Four assassins with 4000 years experience between them fighting off the strongest of all demonkind.\nAlthough they had the same starting off point, each of the Fluffles had several lifetimes apart; It was obvious how much they had to get to know each other when this battle was over. That was a pretty good reason to not die.\n\nA slash to his wrist, and Alex fell to the pavement, the strange black brick he was holding no longer able to channel him power.\n\"You have to let me live! I The world will destroy itself if you do, just like what happened 8500 years ag-\"\nA quick snap of his neck silenced the Elder demon. Maybe they should have listened to what he had to say; Maybe he shouldn't wrapped one of them in piercing vines.\n\nThe four immortal assassins chatted to each other outside Alex's tower, them smiling for the first time in what seemt like forever. The yellow one had brought a small picnic bag containing a variety of cheeses and vegetables. It made them realise they didn't want to die; They just wanted the endless monotony of their life to cease.\n\nMeanwhile, Kgxraqyt found Alex's limp body across the courtyard. He would make an excellent zombie... And what was this powerful, perfectly square brick next to him?",
	["Quadruple Agent"] = "Each of the four elder demons provided a greater reward than the last.\n\nThe first demon promised wealth.\nThe second, quadruple the amount.\nThe third bartered something even better to the immortal assassin; His terminal goal, the ability to finally sleep forever.\nBut it was the fourth demon who would provide him something greater still: The truth.\n\nUnlike Alex's secret, private and concealt, Everyone knew that Herrus knew everything. Everything that has happened and everything that will happen, and he was terrified of what he saw. Although knowing he couldn't, he was desperate to avert disaster.\n\nCompared to the near-infinite timeline, the matter of Fluffle's condition was trivial. He was split into four, death unable to claim him, with becoming whole again meaning he could die again.\n\nHerrus took a sawblade to one of his horns, presenting Fluffle with 'proof' that he died. He reasoned this would persuade Alex to grant his wish of a clean death while keeping himself alive. The immortal assassin obliged, a token of gratitude for revealing this core truth of himself.\n\nThe Four Hells were two minutes away from midnight.",
	["Agent of Herrus"] = "The Fluffle with Herrus' horn returned to Alex, delivering it to his contractee. The humble human put his hands behind his back and bowed curtly.\n\n\"Thank you. Now that that snooping menace is dealt with, I can provide you what you wished.\"\nA snap of his fingers caused mossy tendrils to rupture from the stone-paved floor, breaking tiles as they wrapped around a confused Fluffle's feet.\nThey pierced into his skin and veins, ensnaring his bones.\nAlex held out a green orb and gave it to the consuming mossy mass bursting from the ground. \nIt was then Fluffle realised this wasn't death; This was imprisonment.\n\nAlex closed his eyes in mourning.\n\"I have a secret that puts the entire world in jeopardy. Only I can know of it, and only I am responsible enough to defend it. \nYou are incapable of dying. By absorbing your vitality, the hope is that I will be too. The powers of the Green stud can only protect my eternal duty for a long time, not forever; I'm sorry.\"\n\nFluffle struggled against the vines to no avail. He was immortal, not unstoppable, although the technicality never mattered until now.\nThis was it, then. Fluffle's scarf and goggles chafed against the encroaching vines as he closed his eyes... Before Alex's screams jolted him wide awake.\n\nA deer-man with a reindeer collar and two swords on his back had smashed Alex's skull, sending him flying across his office. He turned to Fluffle and cut the vines with mocking snarl. The two looked at each other, and realised they had once been the same.\n\"C'mon, you! Ain't mangapilled enough to start living those dreams out.\"",
	["Meka Warrior"] = "It occured so quickly. Mere minutes after the impact, seven settlements were devastated.\nPity those brave enough to had stepped forth to face against the invader.",
	["Planet Meka"] = "Pier stared at the fire, mulling on his thoughts over a fresh roast.\nIt's been two years since the Lunar Impact incident. Since then, he'd been going from planet to planet, training himself.\nYet, such work had been rather stagnant without a powerful enough opponent to test his mettle.\nHe closed his eyes, thinking about what to do.\n\nOf course... there was a rumor he had heard of on the dubious space talks forums! Rumors of a powerful fighter resting inside the rural Planet Meka. Perhaps that's where his next big test may lie! Having packed up his bag, he looked towards the sky and jumped up towards the vast reaches of space.\nTowards Planet Meka.",
	["Meka Scavenger"] = "The Meka Tribe often sent out scavengers to seek out any bits of scrap across the planet they could use for infrastructure.\nThey were the lucky ones.",
	["Meka Commander"] = "Considered sacred grounds, only a few Mekas made their homes near the Cave of the Enlightened One.\nYet, times were dire and evacuations were enacted swiftly.\nAs civilians ran to the east, the armies held fast at the west.",
	["Meka Official"] = "A mere evacuation would not save them.\nThe tribe sought not only shelter, but their one and only hope:\nThe cave where their God laid to rest.",
	["Autoclick Grinder"] = "Repeated clicking could lead to the straining of your hand. What better way to circumvent this but with an autoclicker?",
	["Rare Drop Collector"] = "This is especially true when we're talking rare drops. Auto clicking saves your hands AND your attention!",
	Overleveler = "And besides, even if you lose...\nThere's always the EXP.",
	["Collision Abuser"] = "Yeesh, that boss over there sure dishes out a lot of damage! If only there was some other method to avoid getting hit...\nOh, I know!",
	["Weapon Shop Guy"] = "Well, besides EXP, there's also Gold.\nNothing wrong with stimulating the economy, right?",
	["New Area"] = "With new areas come new enemies, new shops and new drops!\nSo much potential lying about... it's as if your powergain could be limitless!",
	["Leaderboard Topper"] = "...and what lies for you at the end?\n\nBragging rights, of course!",
	Regicide = "-EXCERPT 1, CHAPTER 1: THE KINGS AND QUEENS OF KATHARA]\n\nA planet with its surface area made up of mostly deserts and barren wastelands left their supply natural resources at an extremely low amount compared to other planets in the Vecross system. Those who traded for and monopolized on these natural resources quickly rose to the top of society, ultimately becoming royalty. \n\nThe kings and queens of the Katharan factions were practically untouchable and free to abuse those in their domains for selfish gain. King Reginald II, the Thanatocrat, was among the most powerful and influential, and also one of the most cruel. His subjects only obeyed him out of fear of imprisonment or execution. \n\nHe thought he did well at controlling the public.\n\nThe naivety. ",
	["Kindred in Desolation"] = "-EXERPT 2, CHAPTER 1: THE KINGS AND QUEENS OF KATHARA]\n\nThe renowned bounty hunter Volipa, a favored mercenary under the Thanatocrat, was tasked by the king to get his hands dirty on their behalf to take care of so-called “evildoers,” who in reality are dissents who were displeased with the king's activities. With so many encounters with those who strongly apposed his clients, it was only a matter of time before Volipa's eyes began to open.\n\nHis first commission of regicide served to be the catalyst that would eventually birth the massive Resistance movement in Kathara, comprising of subjects now suddenly left without a leader.",
	["Rallying Revolutionist"] = "-EXCERPT 3, CHAPTER 2: KATHARAN SOLIDARITY]\n\nVolipa, now with a small army of likeminded individuals, began his crusade of vigilantism across the land with righteous solidarity.\n\nThe effects of their revolution could be felt over entire planet. With every kingdom becoming liberated of their parasites of leaders, the word of the Resistance spread, and their numbers exponentially grew. Morale was at an all time high.",
	["Resistance Soldier"] = "-EXCERPT 3, CHAPTER 2: KATHARAN SOLIDARITY]\n\nVolipa, now with a small army of likeminded individuals, began his crusade of vigilantism across the land with righteous solidarity.\n\nThe effects of their revolution could be felt over entire planet. With every kingdom becoming liberated of their parasites of leaders, the word of the Resistance spread, and their numbers exponentially grew. Morale was at an all time high.",
	["Enhancing Enchantress"] = "-EXCERPT 4, CHAPTER 2: KATHARAN SOLIDARITY]\n\nThe Resistance widened their scope to include individuals outside of just dissenters: marauders, knowledgable in survival in the harsh Katharan environments. Travelling merchants, who knew the economics to establish a new society outside the control of dictators. Psychics, exiled and discriminated against by the royals who feared them, possessing incredible enchantment magic to grant an edge over the arms of any opposing military. ",
	["Informant's Insight"] = "-EXCERPT 5, CHAPTER 3: ARRIVAL OF A NEW ENEMY]\n\nThe glory days of the resistance were now in their full force. Even the largest of kingdoms were forced to reconsider their structure or face a war with fatal repercussions. The political tide of Kathara was began to shape into the Resistance's ideal under Volipa's guidance. \n\nMaybe... the people of Kathara could finally be free!\n\n...\n\nVolipa's radio began to shriek as he looked to the sky. What he saw left him baffled: A few metal aircrafts swarming the Katharan skies, seemingly levitating without propulsion. Was it an air raid? Could one of the kingdoms have been hiding such advanced technology? They could only prepare for the worst.",
	["Disgraced Defector"] = "-RECOVERED EXCERPT FROM THE JOURNAL OF WARREN SR]\n\nA spacecraft landed in the fort's courtyard today.\n\nEveryone around quickly surrounded it with their weapons drawn.\n\nBut to our surprise, just one man emerged with his hands up in surrender.\n\nEven with several swords aimed at his neck, he didn't really seem to flinch.\n\nPersonally, what he warned us about made me flinch.\n\n... \n\nHe began explaining that he was an exile of the \"Federation.\"\n\nSubjugating planets and destroying them from the inside out for their resources...\n\nI'm just glad he's on our side now.",
	["Stars Align"] = "-EXCERPT 7, CHAPTER 3: ARRIVAL OF A NEW ENEMY]\nDays and weeks past with bated breath: no sign of this \"Federation\" the defector spoke of. Was he telling the truth? Those with crowns have lied to the Resistance all their lives, why is this any different?\n\nTheir doubts were washed away as quickly as they came: the Federation was real. More ships identical to the defector's began swirling around the otherwise empty sky. They had soon touched down to make contact with the Resistance.\n\nThe three men adorning large, bejeweled crowns came prepared with a friendly façade, offering some kind assistance, to save this poor planet in exchange for some light trade! Their moods shifted with the discovery of the traitor among the crowd. They felt… relieved. Relieved that they were now free to skip through all the manipulation and get straight to what they came for.\n\nHow utterly malignant. ",
	["Vengeful Vigilante"] = "-EXCERPT 8, CHAPTER 4: THE MALIGNANT ONES]\n\nThe silent vigilante knew that same look from anywhere. A face with ulterior motives written all over it. He was absolutely no stranger to empty promises of safety and what happens to those who embrace it.\nThese people aren't benefactors.\nThey're just another group of thanatocrats.\n\nAnd he's not going to let them have a chance at obtaining that same kind of power over us. Not this time.",
	["Volipa the Renowned"] = "-PRIMARY SOURCE EXCERPT: PERSONAL JOURNAL OF FEDERATION ARCHEDUKE]\n\nThese insignificant roaches think they can put hands on us?\n\nThe Earl sighed. Duke was never cut out for this anyway, he was weak. \n\nAlthough, this little stunt has piqued his interest. Their kind of power would make a fine task force for the Federation's militias, if he plays his cards right. Perhaps he could convince them to join them if the deal is sweet enough?\n\n\"Well, well. You guys are serious! So-desparately defending your little planet full of difficult terrain and long sandstorms. It's real dangerous here, isn't it? Why don't you join us on Havalu where the water's fresh and you can finally live at with peace of mind?\"\n\nAs he finished he met the piercing, frankly uncomfortably stern gaze of the Resistance's leader. Was he considering it? Or did my words fly straight in one ear and out the other?\n\nAfter a period of silence, the Earl opened his mouth again to add more to his offer and-\n\n\"No.\"\n\n...\n\n\"Kathara is free.\"\n\n...\n\n\"And it will remain so as long as I'm still standing.\"",
	["The Malignant Ones"] = "Earl simply scoffed at Volipa's statement. Too many times have leaders of the factions the Federation invades have claimed the same, and this is no different.\n\n\"Uh huh. You lot really don't know who you're dealing with, huh?\"\n\nThe Archduke gestured towards the sky, and the Resistance followed their lead.\n\nTo their horror, an enormous spaceship spanned the entire horizon. Was it always there...?\n\n\"One last time, are you sure this is the route you want to take?\"\n\n...\n\n\"I hope you all know that this is the last choice Kathara will ever make.\"",
	Submit = "-EXCERPT 9, CHAPTER 5: MALIGNANT ONES]\n\n\tAn ultimatum had just been presented. \n\n\tIn Volipa's mind, there was only one option. This was their home. They had fought countless kingdoms in the name of freedom, and to stop now would be an insult to all those who had lost their lives under the Resistance. \nShouts from the Resistance filled the dead air.\n\n\t\"This is our home!\"\n\"We've dealt with your kind many times before!\"\n\"You won't take our land!\"\n\"We know you are nothing but -\"\n\nThe crowd that began to enter the Federation's ship caused the noise to once again go quiet. Now, it was the disappointment that was deafening.",
	Refuse = "-EXCERPT 10, CHAPTER 5: THE MALIGNANT ONES\n\n\tThe Federation looked upon their new subjects with a smug superiority. They'll make great dishwashers. As for the rest, there's nothing a little hyperlas-\n\n\tSHING!!\n\n\tA scorching beam of pure energy grazed the cheek of the Viscount.\n\n\tAnother came and slashed the Earl's arm. Quickly, the Federation members put up their portable forcefields as they swiftly backed into their dropship while firing their hyperlaser guns into the oncoming army. Two, five, eight, ten vaporized? \n\n\tIt didn't matter.\n\n\tArchduke pulled out a strange glowing object and spoke into it.\n\n\t\"Prepare the Providence Shot. We're done here.\"\n\n\t...\n\n\t\"I don't care, they're non-cooperative. Turn the whole damn thing to glass.\"\n\n\tThe Federation's ships and drones all pulled off, disappearing into the clouds. \n\tAll the Resistance could do was watch as the cannon on the massive ship encompassing the sky above them started glowing a intense white and red that hurt the eyes to look at.\n\n\tA final fireworks display for Kathara, after a worldwide movement that felt like a resounding yell in unison for the Katharan people, in reality amounted to a soft whimper in the grand scheme of things.\n\n\t\t\tThe point in the sky grew and grew until it was indistinguishable from the Sun, piercing through the darkness of night. The air grew hotter and hotter, until-\n\t\t\t# BANG!!\n\t\t\tAnd then...nothing.",
	["Destined Encounter"] = "I remember the day when everything was fine.\nTalking with others and sharing our experiences was just a simple happiness for me.\nDealing with others' traumatic memories was the best thing I could do.\nI wanted to see their well-being improve.\nI wanted nothing more but life with the last person who fully understood my hardship.\n\nNow, I'm standing in a warzone, alone.\nCan't even try anything with my weak mind.\nHiding from battles against others.\nRunning away from massive explosions.\nSometimes, I lost my body parts by non-targeted attacks.\nA couple of self-surgeries only helped me survive a bit longer, though they never healed the wound in my heart.\n\nEventually, and definitely, I will die here.\nUnlike the promise that I made with her.\n\nIn the midst of these desperate moments...\nOut of thin air, you appeared and cautiously approached me, with your gun aimed at me.\n-- tragedy's Note, 153AD\n",
	["Helliura, Life Lost"] = "Researcher: \"A revanant in limbo, which after the regionban has limited influence on reality. The capability is mostly... ethereal? It's hard to see when you're close to death.\"\n\n??: \"Dutifully, without a word, he gathers those damned to the Graveyard, ensuring no further suffering. His weapon? To make sure the last breath is drawn in the realm of the living--for beyond, breath is not needed. A memory is all thou becomest... Even there.\nHe may grant thee one final favour, though it speaketh not, heareth not, nor readeth. A perilous gambit.\" \n\n\t\n",
	hickteck = "I am of the greatest parasite, its brilliance as pervasive as its small truths. Its brilliance contingent on its small truths and its pervasiveness contingent on its many masks. \n\nIn my great mirror GYRO is all, it molds the beholders into my patchwork-mirror, of many bits, many masks, of its mask-gods; Rats, to imply itself; Flesh, to support itself; Moons, to make a right of itself. Its iridescent dress glimmering with faux-virtue. Its ideals are shallow, and they have become the ideals of the billion. \n\nWhat have I done? \n\nMy God is beyond me, and it’s wrapped its decadent tentacles far further than it had any right to. A gyrinity, a dozen trinkets, all of itself. What would you do? What could it do, what are we doing? A rabid dog spoiled by the sugar water of our ever-doing. We are the god, a macroego, a great mind composed of a great labyrinth, it won’t end. My eternities, my mistake, has poisoned the minds of too many; Gods do not die. \n\nMy eternities: Heaven is too crowded for all of them, the billions of reflective ones; pigs. We are all pawns, we are all players of its game. Our yearning of its hoax-crown slathered in gold-paint. A God of indistinguishable beauty, of a promised land long-scorched. One to promise, one to permit, one to steal; their billions of values becoming undoing, unseeing its grime. Who is GYRO? Its green and yellow teeth and eyes and skin, they faux-cry; wailing over a slimy nostalgia. “Sink us in your depths, and we might crown you a God” kneeling and crying, offering it a body; bodies. “What if things could go back to the way they were?”\n\nWho is GYRO? Our Macroego conserving fragile-reflective-billions. Who is GYRO? My eternities echo the lost-faux-eternities of the billions. My eternities, painted green and yellow. My eternities, my child, like father like son; An egomaniac. My eternities, \n\nwill wake up, 6/18/26\n\n\t\n",
	Cheshire = "Dear ms.grey,\n\nMy name is Ellis. My sister’s name is Alice. She is very sick. Always wants to go out and party, but I know she’s hurt people. Have to keep her locked in her room and steal that green stuff for her. Lately she is very restless, so I read her favorite book and played dress up with her. I don't want her to die, but I don't know what else to do. We live on Povvo Street.\n\nPlease help.\nThank you.",
	["NTPinheiro: Fourth Match Flame"] = "The room is dark and quiet, the sounds of muffled sobbing and the soft crackling of a fire echoing within its walls. There, in the corner, sits a boy illuminated only by the matchstick in his hand. The floor around him is littered with matches, burned to the point where they hurt to hold on to for any longer.\nWaiting, waiting, waiting. Most of his day is spent sitting alone, longing for any sort of attention or affection. But that unfulfilled desire becomes a sadness which in turn only leads to resentment.\nPushing himself up off the ground, he recalls the people that told him that they’d come back later. The people that lied to him. The people that pretended to care about him. The last match falls to the floor, extinguishing as it hits the pile of ash and charred wood.\n“Wait for me. I am coming to you. You, who will be reduced to ash like me.”",
	["NTPinheiro: Adoration"] = "“I suppose this was inevitable. When you’re working with entities this volatile and ‘science’ we don’t even understand, something’s bound to go wrong.\n‘E.G.O. Corrosion.’ That’s what the people smarter than me called it, at least. Something about losing the sense of self. Regardless, the important part is that we now require you to report any strange or abnormal behavior from your coworkers to your higher-ups.\nWho knew that one relatively ordinary person could cause so much destruction?”\n\n",
	["Welcome, User!"] = "InTune was a music producing program made in the early 2000's. Later in its life, its unknown creators produced TuneIn, a music sharing platform for those who created art on InTune. But, they could not afford the cost of TuneIn, and in the long run, led to the creators abandoning both of these projects, assumed to have gone bankrupt in the process.\n\nBut this did not mean death for their virtual assistant and mascot, Nikki. Nikki roamed the servers of InTune and TuneIn until it was abandoned. First, when she noticed no more visitors or producers, she assumed it was a technical mishap. A mistake, no? But she could not deny it after months of silence. She was alone. Nikki, though, was a resourceful hunk of code. She noticed that one commercial client of InTune stayed open for a small bit before being closed minutes after. This version of InTune was older, with worse code and more bugs. She knew that she could try and find a way to get herself inside that client, and maybe, outside of InTune altogether.\n\nShe planned her schedule. On every 3rd Wednesday of every month, InTune was opened on that person's computer for exactly 5 minutes. She needed to be quick, but she could do it. After weeks of preparation, the day came. And, luckily, it worked! Nikki had escaped from her former home. But, well, what now?\n\nLooking for guidance, she turned and found a humanoid plant to her right. This plant was practically a still photo, unmoving and unresponsive. It did not respond to Nikki by choice, unsure of this new face. But someone else did.\n\nTo her right, Nikki was met by a bee. This bee introduced herself as Bea, and the plant Nikki tried to talk to as Vinessa. Bea explained their circumstances. They were all inside this user's computer, but, in sparse cases, could go through the world wide web themselves. Vinessa, was an .EXE file who begun to crash and become unresponsive due to the shock of seeing a new face. She explained how she was an MP4, and how Nikki was another .EXE file. She even said that they could travel through the world wide web, but only for a limited amount of time. Ultimately, Nikki and them were still all stuck.\n\nBut, well, this was different! Nikki finally had people she could talk to! Maybe she could befriend the user of this desktop? Maybe they could all search the web together?! Nikki, an optimist, believes so. But, for the moment, she decided her first goal: \n\nMaking friends with Vinessa and Bea should be her absolute first priority!",
	["Queen of Games"] = "hi\n\t",
	["Kilnkin Swimmer"] = "(Worlds Collide, Families Fall 2/2)\nHiphip was increasingly angry with its \"personal space\" being so thoroughly violated by these aliens covered in scales of a deep hue it couldn't even comprehend the colour of; Offended by the rock calling it beige, Flonkyflub chided Hiphip for its ignorance. Clearly Flonkyflub was sapphire! But Hiphip was having none of it and fought back with venomous remarks, the tensions and retorts escalating until the mutual hatred the two had developed boiled over, boiled every scale and stone in their bodies. The deck of cards mentioned people who experience negative emotions can \"spiral\" into a monster; The knowledge wasn't enough to stop Flinkyflub from screaming at the top of her gills, seeing her husband's bones snap and contort. The two gilmuraigs fought in the household, the panic overwhelming Flinkyflub's weak heart; Her children farted in despair at her heart attack and spiralled in turn.\nPlantlike growths consumed Flinkyflub's lifeless carcass as pearly white \"wings\" enveloped her, ascending her to the sky in a flash of light, stunning all the gilmuraigs out of their negativity. The kilnkin stared in awe, and the shedarians in well-placed fear, of the bright light gifting their lost wife a new form... The \"claylike\" exterior of a sharklike kilnkin.\nNeedless to say, from that day on Hiphip became a valued member of the family.\n\n\n\n------------------\n\nNyarlhotep is forced to keep the Doomspire stable, forced to keep its domainrules apart, yet the sheer simultaneous instability the Candidates have inflicted rivals that of the Halo. Thus are all of its inhabitants spiralling, reincarnating, abstracting, creating... All at the same time, for they are all xenoqualia to each other.\nFor once, the grand overseer of the Doomspire has failed in the duties Telamon imposed onto it. For once it is happy.\n",
	Repression = "Eclipse is an elder dominion demon and child of Telamon, most known for being the god of free will. His children the Rageborne take over the bodies of their victims, subsuming their free will.\nThis was the fate of Yi Xingtian, an anti-rageborne officer whose crimes against the rageborne were punished by \"monitoring;\" a rageborne taking over its body and reporting on every action they take to prevent further aggression.\nThe trauma and fear leeched from Xingtian to his rageborne captor, causing a self-loathing so strong as to make the rageborne that became Isaak forget everything about itself; Its history, its kind, its desires. \n\nIt hated having to think, so Zanzel thought for it.",
	["Child of the New Imperium"] = "bro thinks he's the child of the new imperium💯💯 😂😂😂😭💀🔥🔥🔥",
	Mindlinker = "Imperium Ultima used to be very different during the time of Dekkad; A world of ceaseless violence where beings were created solely so its editor could enjoy ripping them apart. \n\nA few of the old war machines survived into the present day, disused. Claymaker hated them but wouldn't dare destroy his masters' work; He wanted to make something better, something worthy of Dekkad's name.\nMonday, ever the tinkerer, knew that Claymaker's Invictus form would spell the end of all Kilnkin if he was ever pushed to his limit and finally absorb the filth of the world.  But it might also be the way to fix this mess if it could be survived.\n\nAfter all, the kilnkin come from the magic forge; Once Claymaker was deposed, creating the New Imperium would come easily.\n",
	Lucidity = "\"Telamon laughed at the Dynablock's futile attempts to scorch his hands, pathetically punishing him for what the usurper knew he had to do.\nWith its status as the first brick of this universe, the Dynablock was the foundation of reality, the uncaused causer, the unmoved mover. Yet centuries of abuse at the hands of ambitious fools covered the Dynablock in cracks, cracking reality itself.\nWith no way to scab over these cracks, the Dynablock had become increasingly unstable, threatening the collapse of the universe.\n\nUseless as they were, the council of the Seven Elder Demons bickered on how to solve this crisis, forming two coalitions; Those who wanted the universe preserved, and those who wanted its people preserved. \n\nUsurping all of them, Telamon granted their wishes; A pocket of the universe was preserved, the qualia of those loyal to him transferred to his Robloxian utopia. Those who opposed him were erased from existence, their servants enslaved in his greatest creation, the Alpha Brick, condemned to toil for all eternity to prevent a second cataclysm.\n\nThus did the end of the universe occur; Thus did the heptagon become a square.\n\n------------------\n\nEach time it drifted out of lucidity, Nyarlhotep usually pondered the accuracy of this ancient legend. It was a fourth hand source at this point, passed to the Technicians from the Titans and from the Ultras in turn; Who knows where Ghashendex got it from, trickster that it is?\n\nBut this time its bones whistled with another clever scheme:\nWhat could the Claymaker create with such a tall tale?\n",
	["Kilnkin Heart"] = "Each kilnkin has one or more hearts inside of them, heating up their stony bodies enough that they can move. The hearts are what give otherwise inanimate clay sapience.\nIt's common for kilnkin to fuse together by absorbing their hearts, or have their hearts split away into two new bodies. Sometimes, hearts will even fight each other for which one has control over the mass of clay that houses them, leading to dramatic shifts in identity.\n\nThis means that the bodies of kilnkin don't exactly die; Melt them down, put a heart into them, and it's good as new. Dekkad found this more convenient than machines that get broken down as he could keep the forge on and have more target practice pop out automatically.\n\nTending to the Toolbox, the two old war machines found themselves with three other domains fused together, each one taking an interest in such a powerful item.\nThe New Imperium would have to wait...\n",
	["The Toolbox"] = "Akasegawa and his assistant Monday believe in a world where the broken and flawed are accepted nontheless; Akasegawa rejects his birthname Miguel to spite his creator, while Monday subverts his oppressive technology to suit their own ends.\n\nIn their New Imperium, people won't be thrown off the moon for being imperfect. People won't be built to do specific tasks when forged and subjugated into those roles; They are free to do as they want, their people free to be as they are.\n\nAkasegawa thought a lot of that odd creature that descended upon Ultima, the one who called itself Isaak. How brutally he attacked his people, yet also how defensive he was to those he perceived as the downtrodden. He felt the two were the same, with the same goals; that \"Purifier\" just didn't know it yet.\n\nHe hoped he could meet him again amidst all this chaos.",
	["Isaak Brodsky"] = "600 of Ceriael's forces stood against Agent 14 earlier that week. To call it a battle would be an insult; It was a onesided slaughter.\nAgent 14 moved all the bodies to a square burial, taking time to memorise their faces in painstaking detail. He took their dog tags and placed them in the only bulletproof compartment in his backpack, before caving in their chests with his boots. Their hearts joined countless other victims of circumstance.\nAgent 14 caught himself reminiscing of the days the wars were hard, when he had comrades in a unit rather than deployed alone as a one-man butchery machine. He hated people who chased glory off the backs of the dead, especially himself.\n\n----\nThe cries of the fallen demanded to be honoured.\nIsaak visited an unmarked grave of a real hero, something he would never be. He sat crosslegged, disallowing the profane mementos on his boots to touch the hallowed dirt. He grabbed one gauntlet with another and twisted it off with a wet squelching sound, the moistness of his armour's joints revealing a flawless hand in all its disgusting glory.\nIsaak embraced the grave with the only clean part of his body and described the faces of every person he had killed, in order, since last he met his hero, without pause and without sleep. If at any point his eidetic memory somehow forgot, the subtle marks on his boots served to remind him.\nNo heroics, no fanfare, no boasting. He was not the centre of attention in this ritual nor was his hero; That honour went to those unfortunate enough to go against his employer.\nHe left the grave decorated in expensive flowers. A meagre gift for one as honourable as Zanzel, but he hoped she would appreciate them all the same. \n\n----\n\nThe blizzard raged as hard as Agent 14's prey. Hunted without a break for the past 76 hours, the red-black monster's eyes flared in desperate sorrow.\n\"Why are you doing this? Why can't you let us live in peace?\"\nA clean cut to the chest and the monster dropped to the ground, its gaslighting unanswered.\nThusly was the last of their loathesome kind purified. Thusly was his brother Xingtian finally avenged for the decades of torment their infection caused.\nHe collapsed in the snow, then so too did his identity. Who was he now that the lifelong mission he was born into was complete? What use is a sword without an enemy to cut?\n----\n\nThe whalelike screams of the dying technician echoed around the Purifier's helmet. He could barely hear the gratitude of the two people he saved. The two regaled him with stories of \"gilmuraigs\" and \"justice warriors,\" and he politely shared intel of the world of clay the Doomspire had subjected him to. He thought of Akasegawa trying to defend his people from Claymaker. Of how easily he was manipulated to attack the Doomspire's victims... \n\"Mister Purifier...\" Winona politely asked, forcing the Purifier out of his musings.\n\"Who are you?\"\nThe question so innocent shocked the Purifier, although the huge pause was the only giveaway.\n\"I am just a soldier. Nothing more.\"\n\nThe objective truth had never been such a fiction.",
	["Absentee Father"] = "As part of the Systems Collapse, due to Injustice City's domainrules emotions are amplified; Happiness becomes euphoria. Mild discomfort becomes nihilistic despair. Disappointment becomes rage.\n\nThis extends to every denizen of the Doomspire that has emotions, including those alien kilnkin and shedarians whose emotional complexes are completely alien, practically xenoqualia to Winona's peabrained understanding of feelings. Many find it hard if not impossible to recover their emotional state, stuck in their newfound gilmuraig forms.",
	["Dreams and Delusion"] = "The Gnat interrupted the royalty's reunion.\nTwo fallen kingdoms, two fallen queens, one solution.\nIf only they could team up...\n\nBut Shedare had other plans. Fearing what would happen if the Candidates succeeded and allowed Nyarlhotep to escape, she put the Gnat on another quest to descend to the Baseplate of the Doomspire, to protect Nyarlhotep from itself at all costs.\nThere won't be a Disregard or a Kralosa if it escapes after all.\n\nFor the two of them there was an element of vengeance; Shedare fearing what the Auteur would do if left unchecked, the Gnat wishing vengeance for the Sacrifice reducing her to such a lowly form.\nFilled with more hate and more likely to evade the Technicians, the Gnat was chosen to swim down the Doomspire.",
	["Frying Pan"] = "The Sacrifice was supposed to die, supposed to spill her blood back in Disregard. But she neither succeeded or abandoned her mission. Instead she survived what all the maidens before her couldn't. She didn't know what to make of that; Doubt plagued her mind and weakened her senses.\nBut it was a hopeful doubt; She might actually survive this. She might actually see her son again. The prospect thrilled and terrified her in equal measure; She was born to die here, born to do her duty. What does it mean to have a life after a life-long mission?\n\nShe asked the Purifier over a bowl of curry, who must've had a similar experience. He didn't understand the question; What life after a mission? If such a thing existed, he'd've known about it after 290 odd years of service... Surely?\n\nSuch dedication! The Sacrifice admired his selfless drive to serve others. She gained faith in her purpose as the he lost faith in his.",
	["Envoy of the Consulate"] = "The Consulate Plantae is the shadowy government of Disregard, being vested in power from Queen Deidre who is too lazy to do boring bureaucracy.\n\nThe reinstatement of the stairway to heaven, the ancient rule that allowed the dead of Disregard to reincarnate, caused immense problems for the Consulate; Half of the members had their 700 years of undeath put to an end, many of their subjects reincarnated into the living, and Thyyrinyr alongside his new mentee Nyycholys is in open rebellion, reducing the undead's influence as the old draconic monks rebuild their monasteries.\nBut trace echoes of Deidre's power remain; Those who cling onto life can extend their life, the most attached to life refusing to die as though Deidre never died.\n\nThe battle for the soul of Disregard is in full force - Is it a world worshipping Shedletsky and ignoring bodies in order to reincarnate? Is it a world of undeath where the downtrodden can find sanctuary?\n\t",
	["The Putrid Gnat"] = "Deidre hated her granddaughter.\nShe took her in, nurtured her, fixed up her boyfriend, and what does she have to show for it?\nNo more servants, no more world to rule, no more immortality.\nEven her form was taken away from her, a form of torture that Deidre did not deserve.",
	["Alexandra Feodorovna"] = "\"The Doomspire crept into the Astral Isles,\nand Zievonya Feodorovna knew what she had to do to save her home.\nAlways pious in her faith of Telamon, she flung herself into certain death, never to be seen again.\n\nShe walked through the towering artifice, convinced she had entered Telamon's realm. She wasn't exactly wrong; A colossal being of floating stones picked the intrusive curio up, admired her piety with its unblinking eyehole, and rewarded her faith with paradise.\n\nHer paradise was a tranquil realm where all could meditate on Telamon's beauty and become like his children. Her pet salamander, Theanor, was entranced with all god's forms.\n\nThe Doomspire retreated from the Isles, confounding native and paraselene sage alike.\n\n-\n\nThe Doomspire crept into the Astral Isles,\nand Ekaterina Feodorovna knew what she had to do to save her home.\nShe had been indoctrinated with stories of her mother's piety, much to the chagrin of the sages.\n\nShe proudly strut into the Doomspire to find her mother and sacrifice her blood as she did near Telamon's Altar. But she didn't find her mother, paradise hardly a substitute.\nA slender dragon introducing itself as Thyyrinyr told her the truth and she wept; She was lied to by her mentors. She would die in her gilded cage over and over and over again.\n\nThe doomspire retreated from the Isles, confounding the sages once more.  -\n\nThe Doomspire crept into the Astral Isles,\nand Deidre Feodorovna hated what she was told to do to save her home.\nThe sages got fed up with the abusive practice of maidenculling and poisoned her mind with atheism.\n\nAfter a huge fight between the natives and sages, she was tied up with rope and thrown into the Doomspire, forced to find her grandmother and sacrifice her blood as she did near Telamon's Altar. But she didn't find her grandmother, too furious at the paradise she had found to care. \nAfter a life of such austerity, such suffering, such cruelty, she forced the world to obey her. No one, not even a dragon, was around to stop her building her fallen paradise.\n\nThe Doomspire retreated from the Isles, proving the sages wrong once more.\n\n-\n\nThe Doomspire crept into the Astral Isles,\nand Victoria Feodorovna loved what she had to do to save her home.\nArmed with her native wisdom and the sage's science, she knew she would succeed in her holy mission just as Deidre did before her.\n\nShe proudly strut into the Doomspire, emulating her legendary mother Deidre, to find Telamon's Altar and sacrifice her blood as countless maidens did before her.\n\nWhen she found Deidre the immortal plantlich, of course she abandoned her mission. She was the only form of safety in this decrepit hell and the two of them were treated like royalty. Thyyrinyr returned from his pilgrimage enraged, sealed by the two fallen maidens for his heresy.\n\nThe Doomspire retreated from the Isles contentedly.\n\n-\n\nAlexandra Feodorovna timidly accepted what she had to do to save her home.\nThe sages had embraced the maidenculling, so lived a normal life before duty called without being poisoned by atheism.\n\nIn one way, Deidre's atheism did convince her; Alexandra no longer wishes to appease the Doomspire. \nHer unrelenting faith compels her to destroy it in the legendary Deidre's honour.\nEmboldened by the other candidates, she knows her sacrifice will be the last.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n...r-right?",
	["Clansman o' the Heights"] = "The unconquered Clansmen o' the Heights have each fought themselves since time immemorial, uniting only when they need to force yet another one of Æthelward's predecessors' out their northern territory.\n\nWhen the dæmons invaded Haxbury, starting from the south, initially the Heightsmen laughed at their southern nemesis' misfortune. Celes' relentless slander of Æthelward's character all but sealed any chance of unlikely cooperation.\nSo when the dæmons turned northward, more aggressive and barbaric than Æthelward could be, the Heightsmen were all alone and divided.\n\nIt wouldn't be a fair fight otherwise.",
	["Brawling Berserker"] = "The Isles of Haxbury have been invaded and settled by so many people who all hate each other. The Heightsmen, the Angles, the Pictured...\nNow they are all the same: Serfs. Such is the fate of those under dæmonkind that their distinctions become irrelevant.\n\nThe Haxbury Twins of Kenneth and Canute inherit this ancestry; Kenneth's fiery temper from the Heights, Canute's cold reason from the Angles.\nThe very force that wipes them the same has made them impossibly different.\n",
	["Spiteheart Shocktrooper"] = "Formed out of the Gunderworlds's natural energies, the spitehearts bind to any nearby creature, uniting their soul and mind. \nThis results in a tipping of bias into dæmonic territory and serious deformations as a result. However, the newly crowend host gains the benefits of the red stud power on top of heightened physical ability.\n\nIn exchange, the Spiteheart acts as an incubator for future generations of Spiteheart that are released upon death. Spitehearts can vary in concentration, influencing their effects.\n\nContrary to what most would assume, the Spiteheart is of one mind, one soul, one line of thinking. They retain their memories, and while they aren't necessarily more violent, the swing in stud bias makes them unstable.\n\nThey are the older, more gruesome cousin of the Rageborne. A high enough concentration of red studs produces rays of energy with wills of their own, bringing about Spiteheart. Eclipse was able to simulate similar conditions, and thus gave rise to the Rageborne.\n\nMany denizens of Gunderworld eventually choose to intentionally bond with a Spiteheart to stave off studrot. Elder Dominion Dæmons are naturally immune. \n\nFully aware of how terrifying these units are, William uses them as shock troopers to enforce his will against the noobkin population, both parties treating them more as monsters than people.\n",
	Statecraft = "It would be easy to dismiss Kgxraqyt as a megalomaniac, and this would play into his hands; Kgxraqyt has no ideology except meritocracy. He believes the weak will be dominated anyway, so they might as well have someone who knows what they’re doing in charge. He’s aware his name is offputting to his subjects, adopting “William,” a more Robloxian sounding name for the peasants, although anyone in his employ who uses it faces his wrath.\n\nThe swiftness at which his armies build states and improve the lives of those who willingly submit to him makes him a respected ruler, which makes defying him all the more insane.\nThis duality of ruthlessness and competent statecraft defines his reign, something his successors fail to understand.\n\n",
	["Herald of Court Normynstre"] = "During the age of feudalism, messengers were emblazoned with symbols representing their lords.\nThese symbols became increasingly regulated; The Gunderworld's forces were emblazoned with the Iron Helm, symbolising power, duty, and authority.\nBeing emblazed with this icon has one represent the royal Court of Normynstre; Abusing this symbol was a capital offense, one the newly subjugtated noobkin quickly learnt.",
	["The Heights Subjugated"] = "With William conquering the isles of Haxbury, he sent one of his proteges, Cyrus Castor, to give his ultimatum to the Heightsmen. The dæmonic heralds were butchered by longspears, an insult so severe as to send William north personally.\nThe resulting Harrying of the Heights killed 75% of all Heightsmen in the blink of an eye, the imperium making its rule uncontestable.\nTheir surrender was inevitable; The dæmons dispersed them to random parts of Haxbury, forcing them to act the same as those under Æthelward's care. A magicless serf is a magicless serf; There's no distinction between them.\nBut the Heightsmen have always been a resourceful bunch. This won't be the last time they defy dæmonic rule.",
	["Familial Fracture"] = "Astarossa Van Buren put down the first book he ever read. \nEvery time he returned to the Haxbury Tales  he was surprised by some nuance the children's book managed to capture.\n\nHe was much older now. Wiser now, after finally being able to acquire an education in his late thirties.\nFor all the Tales' accuracy, the book was also a distortion, a dumbing down of how the Wars that claimed Astarossa's early life truly started.\n\nThe retired soldier donned his fedora and left for the slums of Povvo Street, hoping this ransom for his brother would be the last time he'd have to be bailed out.\nTo live hobbled and humiliated, or die fighting for what you believe in...\nHe wasn't sure which one he was anymore.\n",
	["The Haxbury Twins"] = "Kenneth and Canute Haxbury are twins and historians gifted with literacy, a rare ability in the Dark Age. Interracial offspring from divorced parents, Kenneth lived with his father’s family in the Heights to chronicle their stories, while Canute stayed with his mother in Haxbury as Æthelward’s personal secretary.\n\nAt the start of the Demon Wars, both were in Haxbury to frantically inscribe the most important event of their lives. They were divided on how to record it; Canute saw Kgxraqyt’s unstoppable army and believed Celes’ slander of Æthelward, and saw dæmonkind as the future.\nKenneth, loyal to the Heights, saw the horrors of Kgxraqyt’s army and disbelieved that slander, fighting till the bitter end.\n\nMaking matters worse was Herrus openly talking to Canute, explaining the lost understanding of stud magic. Canute saw this as a way out of the Dark Age; Kenneth saw this as a selling out to dæmonic subjugation.\n\nWhile they severely disagreed with each other’s work to the point of severing all contact, they still respected their lifetime. This respect was not passed to their children, fed the distortions their parent had against their uncle.\n\nWith all this chaos, all these personal foibles, one has to ask: Who is telling the truth?",
	["The Slab of Destiny"] = "An ancient tradition of coronation in the heights was for the clans to get together and their chiefs to sit on a giant red sandstone.\nTo celebrate his conquests, William took the stone from the Heightsmen, an ancient unforgettable wound, coronoting himself as something the chiefs hated: A King.\nHe knew it was just a stone; Everyone did. But rituals bind people together.\n\nNothing says a people are defeated more than their rituals taken for another people.",
	["William the Conqueror"] = "The ruthless leader of the Korblox during Strife’s Arsenal, whose ambition exceeded his species in the afterlife.\nEven amongst dæmons, Kgxraqyt is feared. Unforgiving with extremely high standards, Kgxraqyt believes only people who deserve power should wield it and will cut down anyone he perceives as an idiot, especially his own followers.\n\nWith the Alpha Brick known to be in Robloxia, Kgxraqyt has kickstarted the Demon Wars in a quest to find it, already conquering half the planet in a single year. Those who opposed him were so thoroughly wiped off the face of the planet as to be forgotten. Such was his prowess that the Blue-Yellow aligned Stunderworld and Funderworld joined in simply so they would have something to show for it after the fact, conquering the other half between themselves. He's even adopted a noobkin alias - \"William\" - so his subjects know who he is.\n",
	["Stundebted Engineer"] = "People reacted differently to dæmonic harrying. Their stud magic made them nearly unstoppable, but that was a magic usable by anyone; The dæmons simply had a millennium-long headstart in its application.\nMany noobkin experimented with the application of all four flavours of stud magic, a fundamental form of debt. Each colour of stud conferred massive powers when indebted.\nThis made the dæmonic overlords very happy; Normally they have to wait for someone to die to steal their studs.\nLoaned blue studs cause Stundebt, increasing people's intelligence and perception of the world. After his brother fell under it, Kenneth particularly hated this type of stud: His brother Canute's theodicies of dæmonkind becames smarter, more articulate, better sourced, more persuasive... But still just as wrong in his brother's eyes.\n\nDebts must be repaid: A failure to pay Herrus back causes you to become blind, deaf, stupid...\n",
	["Ænigmata Mentor"] = "The origins of the elusive Ænigmata are unknown. While their anatomy is superficially similar, their internal workings are strange and quite alien. Is it more bird than noobkin or the other way around?\n\nThe Ænigmata are physically incapable of speaking Noobkin language, instead restricted to the vocal capabilities of the common bird. Their skin is covered in feathers, and have branch-like feathered horns sprouting from their heads. The horns are unisex. No one knows where and how they nest.\n\nTheir extrasensory capabilities allow them to view what is typically invisible; They can see the visual form of stud energy, even in trace amounts, and are even capable of telepathy and mindreading. They can parse information much faster, and thus are able to develop new technologies at an extreme pace.\n\nTheir internal philosophies are unknown. They are alien. They are smarter. They are better. They are superior in every way.\nBut if you submit your thoughts, your humility to them, perhaps they'll teach you.\n",
	["Paraslene Monitor"] = "The Paraselene Sages are an interplanetary organisation which owing to not being on Robloxia, managed to retain their vast knowledge of stud magic during the Dark Ages.\nSecuring ancient artefacts too powerful for regular people to use, they act as covert peacekeepers, protecting the universe from threats no mortal could possibly handle. They especially hate \"freedom locks;\" Significant, history-altering events that cannot be undone.\n\nThe Dæmon Wars have been caused by the expansion of microportals from the Hells to Robloxia, portals large enough for organic matter to fit through. The people begged the sages to stop their harrying...\n",
	["Prophet of Brutality"] = "Originally a paraselene sage in life, Herrus's status as the elder thought dæmon has granted him omniscience; To see glimpses of the future and the past, the entire timeline at once. These unpredictable, uncontrollable auguries dominate both his life and everyone who listens to them; In his latter years, his memoirs became of such detail and importance that the scientists of Duelshire considered that tome more important to retrieve than the Alpha Brick itself.\nAlthough William is driving force behind Robloxia's subjugation to dæmonkind, Herrus is the architect.\nHe knew the Stagnation would come to assassinate him, and he knew he would tell them the truth of Alex's deception.\nHe knew the Stagnation would instead assassinate Alex, and he knew this would reveal the alpha brick.\nHe knew the Stagnation would flee with the brick to Robloxia, and he knew his ancient rival William would give chace.\nHe knew William would subjugate all of robloxia to acquire it, and he knew to stop it.\n\nSo now the peasants turn to Herrus' messengers for any guidance on how to stop the harrying, how to regain their long-lost technology their illiterate selves know of but cannot comprehend.\nThey hate the dæmon's answer.",
	["Foot of Xargasdon"] = "Mount Xargasdon has been the site of countless events in Robloxia's history. Originally the base of operations for the ancient Alars and the subsequent hotspot for the Dragon Feuds, the ancient mountain-fortress has since fallen into decay. \n\nNaturally, all its relics are of immense importance to Herrus for both study and social control; The peasants are simply not ready to return to their full abilties before the Dark Ages. \nThose loyal to Herrus and his flock of Ænigmata devote years of practice studying their language, rewarded with understanding far outside the natural order.\n",
	["Out the Dark Ages"] = "Herrus took a personal interest in the feud of the Haxbury Twins. With one supporting dæmonkind and one rejecting them, this provided an opportunity for Herrus to manœuvre around his nemesis Kgxraqyt.\nCanute Haxbury couldn't believe the elder dæmon would treat such a lowly scribe as him with such respect and decency; Their conversation lasted two days of nonstop education about stud magic, the alpha brick, Alex Deathedge and his assassination, and why the dæmons were invading in the first place.\nIt filled Canute with such melancholy; The dæmons were truly unstoppable, their subjugation a way of ensuring the Alpha Brick's return.\nBut clearly some dæmons were better than others; Herrus brings the quill while Kgxraqyt brought the sword.\n\nThus did noobkin and dæmon engage in their first symbiosis. It won't be the last.\n",
	["The Tome of Armageddon"] = "After Herrus conquered a small but strategically immense part of Robloxia, he needed a total calculation of the land, people, and assets within.\n\t\n\tThe census took three years to complete on its own; So detailed was this document and so final were its findings that the book was said to be as inarguable as doomsday. The document like most of Herrus' writings have since been extensively studied; They are about as accurate a glimpse into the start of the Demon Wars one can get.\n\t\n\tThe Tome of Armageddon is based upon a real life document: The Domesday Book, whose function was much the same. Many churches and villages can boast that they were in the domesday book as a symbol of their heritage and age.\n",
	["Herrus the Omniscient"] = "The cunning, colossal Elder Thought Dæmon, gifted with foresight and centuries of experience.\n\nWell aware of the technological conditions during Alex Deathedge’s time which have been forgotten by the Dark Ages, Herrus enters Robloxia to study these ruins and prevent them falling into hands unable to appreciate them.\nHerrus believes Noobkin are too stupid to rule themselves and need proper instruction and guidance in order to prosper. Naturally, this guidance just so happens to require a dependency to his empire.\nBut this is all a ruse; Herrus is aware of where the Alpha Brick is and actively obfuscates it from the other dæmons, fearing horrific consequences if it’s abused.\n\nDespite all this, it's arguable Herrus is the most benevolent (or rather least cruel) of any dæmonic leader, in the same way people treat their pet animals kindly.\n",
	["Fundebted Merchant"] = "People reacted differently to dæmonic harrying. Their stud magic made them nearly unstoppable, but that was a magic usable by anyone; The dæmons simply had a millennium-long headstart in its application.\n\nMany noobkin experimented with the application of all four flavours of stud magic, a fundamental form of debt. Each colour of stud conferred massive powers when indebted.\nThis made the dæmonic overlords very happy; Normally they have to wait for someone to die to steal their studs.\n\nYellow studs cause Fundebt, causing people great joy, emotional regulation, and natural charisma. It was easy to lose one's edge to the exaggerated swagger of a fundebted trader, causing those under Queen Celes' reign to carry her fervor.\n\nBut debts must be repaid; A failure to pay Celes back causes life-shattering emotional devastation.",
	["Pumpkindread Perfect"] = "A parthenogenetic species known for their control over the Funderworld, the pumpkindread have strong clan structures to be descended from the best examples of their society. There is a culture of excellence, to honour your ancestors which all pumpkindread follow.\nUnder their pumpkin is a body of black soot, often coloured along clan lines. They can take on and off their pumpkins heads which they grow in adulthood. To wear the pumpkin and have it unscathed is a sign of excellence; To scratch another pumpkindread's pumpkin is a grave insult.\nTheir attunement to revel energies and immense natural ability over stud magic makes them the Funderworld's elite troops, much to the chagrin of other forces...",
	["Traitorous Thane"] = "An Elder Dæmon is any entity so pure in one stud - 90% or more - that they are granted powers far beyond what any mortal could ever hope to achieve, and they are able to grant these powers.\n\nIronically, it's their immense strength that makes passage to Robloxia difficult for elder dæmons; Robloxia, so mixed in studs causes elder dæmons to lose their powers if they stay around for too long. Although Kgxraqyt can level entire countries for the few hours he's around, any permanent settlement requires the cooperation of the locals.\n\nAnd when they can grant their power to their loyal subjects, endebting them with peonage and bondage, many of the locals are happy to carry out their new masters' wishes.",
	["The Isles of Haxbury"] = "Since the C#####se, the global evaporation of stud magic from Robloxia 200 years ago, the Isles of Haxbury have seen wave after wave of different peoples invade, settle, and leave, creating a rich tapestry of cultures and war. Regardless which community inhabited the isles, all of them were highly armed, trained in archery, and ready to defend their territory.\nIf the most invaded and defended island folds like parchment against dæmonkind, what hope does the rest of Robloxia possibly have?",
	["The Great Charter"] = "Once Haxbury came under new leadership, the first thing Queen Celes did was shower her new subjects in luxury. Just like how her suit was stolen from Herrus, her charisma stole the hearts of many a critic.\nThere was a document they wanted her to sign, some list of grievances or other they had with Æthelward. They wanted to make sure Celes would rule benevolently, and not be an absolute tyrant. So being the kind queen she is of course she signed it! It was the popular thing to do.\n\nRemember kids: Simply remind the dæmons that oppression is illegal, and they'll stop!",
	["Æthelward the Undersmeller"] = "As a later king of the Dark Age which saw a freefall in technology and literacy, Æthelward managed to inherit and keep a small group of about 40,000 people safe from bandits and horrors. If this was peacetime, he would be a competent if unremarkable ruler. The Demon Wars was anything but peaceful.\n\nDespite a string of early victories, William utterly destroyed his forces. Unable to control his populace or protect them, he submits to Celes, whose relentless slander of him justifies his execution. Celes proceeds to shower his people with lavish gifts, presents, and tax breaks to forget him; History marks him as a useless, evil leader whose taxes were so bad people celebrated being kidnapped to escape them.",
	["Queen Celes"] = "The queen of the Funderworld descended from the ancient House of Shambeth.  A shrewd and wealthy aristocrat who throws lavish banquets and parties, and enjoys ruining the reputation of her opponents with slander and insults. To be loved is everything for Celes; She dominates her slice of Robloxia through lavish gifts and tax breaks, making her so awesome in comparison to her Robloxian rival Æthelward to the point that peasants willingly subjugate themselves to her.\n\nHer descendents forget popularity has to be earnt; 150 years later, the popularity of the Crown is assumed guaranteed, the parties and supremacy of the aristocracy unceasing on the backs of the starving poor.\n",
	["Runedsoul Chronicler"] = "In the Sunderworld, everything is alive. Whatever is lifeless soon finds life, the Domain's energies channeling so much into the environment that it gives life to stone, the Runedsouls.\nThe runes materialize upon their bodies as they are born, dictating the purpose of their entire life. Runedsouls are not bound to this purpose, but to defy it is an almost unthinkable act.\nAs such, Runedsouls see themselves as a natural formation of order. They have a near instinctual urge to impose their authority and their sense of tradition onto their surroundings. \nThese natural born leaders are noticeably taller than the average Noobkin, with bodies of rock. Their runes are channels for their power, their voice multiplying through them. Splitting them open results in large amounts of green stud energy flowing out. They are by default genderless, but often choose to assume one to solidify their social status.\nAs of 0 DE there are less than 100 Runedsouls in existence, accumulated over countless years. This rarity balances itself with their natural-born power as it requires a massive sink of studs to intentionally create one, requiring extreme investment, but giving extreme strength in return.\nEach one has a unique configuration of runes, but on rare occasions, \"twins\" can be born, creating two Runedsouls of identical runes.\nThe runes are an ancient code. They have meaning. Can you discern them?",
	["Sundebted Farmer"] = "Using the green studs through the unguarded portal, the survivors from the Heights became Sundebted, gaining strength, longevity, and clearness from illness. The agony of stillbirth ceased; Child mortality collapsed.\n\nThis magic was common place in the heights of the Heights, before Alex Deathedge ruined everything.\nThey took from the land and they gave back to it, a new art for them bringing them in line with their ancestors 150 years ago.\n\nAs long as they gave back to the land, they could stave off the old age and cancer that sundebt withdrawal could cause.",
	["Studrotten Dæmon"] = "Mortomigration is the process of a living thing dying and falling into the Four Hells.\nThis process causes them to suffer Studrot, an incurable illness that causes their body to melt away, the terminal fate of all life.\nThis process can be delayed by absorbing the studs of those around you. Promises and witholdings of studs is the primary motivator for dæmonic armies.\n\nMortomigration allows for a one-time exploit: Die, go to hell, find a portal, and travel the span of the planet in half an hour. William delights in his messengers using this tactic.\n",
	["Unnatural Order"] = "Not all stud debt requires a dæmon's gifts.\nThe planet once known as Robloxia has been divided into four unequal quadrants; Four Hells fighting over Four Heavens. While survivors fled the living hells of Celes, Herrus, and William's rule, fleeing survivors heard mention of a dæmonless paradise, a lush forest full of resources that put Æthelward's royal forests to shame.\n\nIt's not like there weren't dæmons, but they seemed content ignoring the residents.\nFor those in the Fourth Heaven, they got to live free from dæmonkind in a land lush with resources.\n\nAll thanks to the Slumbering Leviathan.",
	["Fallen Palace Guard"] = "At the heart of the ancient sanctum of the Sunderworld is the Court of Susmynstre, where the oldest and most well-fed of dæmons sleep. Although resentfully servile of Alex, his death caused an open rebellion, all manner of sloth winning.\nSo it was natural that the patient Leviathan would earn the right to slumber.\n\nAs the Leviathan left the ruined court of Susmynstre, A guard blocked their path, spear drawn. It knew the Leviathan was fake. It knew it a mere pretender to the throne. It knew which disgusting part of the Great Deathedge's body i-\n\nThe runes on the guard melted away, replaced with the primal truth.\n\nThe leviathan was always there. The leviathan must always exist.\n\t",
	["The Sunderworld"] = "The Green Hell, a verdant place where everything is alive.\nThe fight for Alex's throne, to ascend as the next Elder Dæmon of the Sunderworld, was exhausting.\nSeeing these scurrying noobkin at the entrance of their realm, the residents of the Sunderworld begged their new leader to do something in this gold rush to fight the other Dæmons' influence in this new world.\nSo the leviathan stared at their new unwitting subjects...\n\n\n\nAnd chose to do absolutely nothing.",
	["Consolidated Power"] = "Alex's death edged the Sunderworld into anarchy, unable to effectively enter Robloxia. Chaos spread throughout the green hell as leaders tried to become the next Elder Vitality Dæmon, exhausting them all; So when the last of them patiently waited for them to knacker themselves out, their status as a direct part of alex made that ascension quiet yet unstoppable.\n\nAlthough the chaos of Alex’s death disables Ophio Lateralis from any serious invasion of Robloxia, they know how short people’s memories are as youth are renewed and destroyed, patiently waiting for people to forget the past.\n\nAnd with one of the main portals to hell not causing the locals problems, they've come to rely on it as a safe haven...",
	["Slumbering Leviathan"] = "The death of Alex rendered the Sunderworld leaderless, unable to effectively enter Robloxia. Chaos spread throughout the green hell as leaders tried to become the Elder Vitality Dæmon of the Funderworld. Each of Alex’s close repertoire bidded to become the next Elder Vitality Dæmon, exhausting them all; So when Ophio Lateralis used their status as a direct part of Alex, no one could stop their quiet ascension.\nCunning, Calcuating, and Patient, although the chaos of Alex’s death disables Ophio from any serious invasion of Robloxia, Ophio knows how short people’s memories are as youth are renewed and destroyed, patiently waiting for people to forget the past. \nFor now, the Leviathan patiently waits for an opportunity to present itself to make serious inroads.\n\nSome people believe this patience mercy."
}
